{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P3PSZmz2zmnjNUjXnzsT6j","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.layout\n2\t  \"Phase 6c (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §4):\n3\t   the de Bruijn register and stack kernels reconstruct the canonical\n4\t   frame of the register machine through their layouts, and lower it\n5\t   back.\n6\t\n7\t   Static half, per segment A: `segment` derives R(A) and H(A) and reads\n8\t   off the register pairing (`phys`, the restricted inverse `virt`, the\n9\t   kernel's `live` as live-out with tail boundaries `[]`), the stack\n10\t   correspondence (`h->a`, `a->h`, every `:push` removed) and the operand\n11\t   layout `stack-layout` (the values pushed and not yet consumed while\n12\t   control is inside a pc's expression). A `space` indexes segments by\n13\t   the kernels' image identities, R and H, which are checksums: A is the\n14\t   only code identity.\n15\t\n16\t   Dynamic half: `lift-state` reads a kernel's wait entry, parked record\n17\t   or reified payload as the canonical `act` or `tail` payload the\n18\t   semantic-register evaluator mints (`{:segment A :pc :env :window :k\n19\t   :deliver}`, `{:segment A :site :k :deliver}`, engine fields carried);\n20\t   `lower-state` is its inverse. The register kernel's return\n21\t   destinations are recovered from A, never from the physical `:dest`;\n22\t   the stack kernel's operand stack is sliced `[previous-base, base)` per\n23\t   frame and lowered with cumulative bases. `E` is the free environment\n24\t   merged under the chain's positional frames (§4.4); the inverse reads\n25\t   each frame back from `E` by the chain, never the free environment.\n26\t\n27\t   Task level: `canonical-task` presents a quiescent kernel as a\n28\t   semantic-register machine for `yin.vm.ucf.rows/lift-task`;\n29\t   `kernel-task` restores a machine `rows/lower-task` produced into a\n30\t   fresh kernel; `lift-task` and `lower-task` compose them with the row\n31\t   carrier, the lower refusing what a kernel cannot hold before any\n32\t   stream is attached. A layout never runs code, never fills a binding\n33\t   from the receiver and never invents a safepoint (§4.5).\"\n34\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n35\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n36\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n37\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as register]\n38\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as stack]\n39\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n40\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n41\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n42\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n43\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n44\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.derive :as derive]\n45\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n46\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n47\t\n48\t\n49\t(defn- refuse!\n50\t  [status kind data]\n51\t  (throw (ex-info \"Layout refused\" (merge data (assoc {} :yin.k/status status :yin.k/kind kind)))))\n52\t\n53\t\n54\t;; =============================================================================\n55\t;; Static half: one segment\n56\t;; =============================================================================\n57\t\n58\t(defn- operands\n59\t  \"The register operands of an A tuple, destination first, then its uses\n60\t   in table order.\"\n61\t  [t]\n62\t  (into (if-some [r (code/rd t)] [r] []) (code/uses t)))\n63\t\n64\t\n65\t(defn- register-operands\n66\t  \"The `:reg`/`:regs` operands of an R tuple in table order (the `:live`\n67\t   slot is `:data`, never paired).\"\n68\t  [t]\n69\t  (into []\n70\t        (mapcat (fn [[[_ kind] x]] (case kind :reg [x] :regs x [])))\n71\t        (map vector (get rcode/opcode-table (nth t 0)) (rest t))))\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t(defn register-pairs\n75\t  \"`[pc virtual physical]` for every register operand of every pc: A's\n76\t   tuple and R's name their registers in the same slots (phase-5 §2.4).\"\n77\t  [v image]\n78\t  (into []\n79\t        (mapcat (fn [pc]\n80\t                  (map (fn [x s] [pc x s])\n81\t                       (operands (nth v pc))\n82\t                       (register-operands (nth (:instructions image) pc)))))\n83\t        (range (count v))))\n84\t\n85\t\n86\t(defn- phys-maps\n87\t  \"Per body, `{virtual physical}` read off the pairs; the first pc that\n88\t   names a virtual wins (register-pairing checks they agree).\"\n89\t  [bodies pairs]\n90\t  (reduce (fn [acc [pc x s]]\n91\t            (let [b (code/body-index bodies pc)]\n92\t              (if (contains? (nth acc b) x) acc (assoc-in acc [b x] s))))\n93\t          (vec (repeat (count bodies) {}))\n94\t          pairs))\n95\t\n96\t\n97\t(defn correspondence\n98\t  \"§4.3 static item 1: H with every `:push` removed corresponds one to one,\n99\t   in order, with A. Answers `{:a->h [h-pc …] :h->a {h-pc a-pc}}`.\"\n100\t  [h]\n101\t  (reduce (fn [acc hpc]\n102\t            (if (= :push (nth (nth h hpc) 0))\n103\t              acc\n104\t              (-> acc\n105\t                  (update :a->h conj hpc)\n106\t                  (assoc-in [:h->a hpc] (count (:a->h acc))))))\n107\t          {:a->h [] :h->a {}}\n108\t          (range (count h))))\n109\t\n110\t\n111\t(def ^:private pushing-ops\n112\t  \"The parse nodes whose children before the current one are pushed:\n113\t   `:call` (the operator and earlier operands), `:ffi-call` (earlier\n114\t   operands) and `:stream-put` (the target, while the value runs).\"\n115\t  #{:call :ffi-call :stream-put})\n116\t\n117\t\n118\t(defn- stack-layouts\n119\t  \"§4.3 static item 2 for every pc of every body: `{pc [virtual …]}`,\n120\t   bottom to top, over the parse tree's ancestors outermost first.\"\n121\t  [v bodies]\n122\t  (letfn [(walk\n123\t            [out node pending]\n124\t            (let [out (assoc out (:pc node) pending)\n125\t                  pushes? (contains? pushing-ops (:op node))\n126\t                  uses (when pushes? (code/uses (nth v (:pc node))))]\n127\t              (reduce (fn [out [i child]]\n128\t                        (walk out child (if pushes? (into pending (take i uses)) pending)))\n129\t                      out\n130\t                      (map-indexed vector (:children node)))))]\n131\t    (reduce (fn [out body] (walk out (:expr body) [])) {} bodies)))\n132\t\n133\t\n134\t(defn segment\n135\t  \"The static facts of one admitted A vector `v`, for both kernels.\"\n136\t  [v]\n137\t  (let [bodies (code/parse v)\n138\t        r (derive/register-image v)\n139\t        h (:image (derive/stack-image v))\n140\t        pairs (register-pairs v r)]\n141\t    (merge {:vector v\n142\t            :address (jing/segment-key v)\n143\t            :bodies bodies\n144\t            :analysis (analysis/analyze v)\n145\t            :register r\n146\t            :register-id (rcode/register-hash r)\n147\t            :stack h\n148\t            :stack-id (dcode/image-hash h)\n149\t            :pairs pairs\n150\t            :phys (phys-maps bodies pairs)\n151\t            :layouts (stack-layouts v bodies)}\n152\t           (correspondence h))))\n153\t\n154\t\n155\t(defn space\n156\t  \"Segments by A, and A by each kernel's image identity. `segments` is a\n157\t   seq of `segment` results or of A vectors.\"\n158\t  [segments]\n159\t  (reduce (fn [acc s]\n160\t            (let [s (if (map? s) s (segment s))\n161\t                  a (:address s)]\n162\t              (-> acc\n163\t                  (assoc-in [:segments a] s)\n164\t                  (update-in [:register (:register-id s)] (fnil conj #{}) a)\n165\t                  (update-in [:stack (:stack-id s)] (fnil conj #{}) a))))\n166\t          {:segments {} :register {} :stack {}}\n167\t          segments))\n168\t\n169\t\n170\t(defn segment-of\n171\t  \"The segment A names in `space`.\"\n172\t  [space a]\n173\t  (or (get-in space [:segments a])\n174\t      (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied :segment {:yin.k/segment a})))\n175\t\n176\t\n177\t(defn- image-segment\n178\t  \"The segment whose `kind` image is `ident`: an identity is a checksum,\n179\t   so two A deriving one image are ambiguous and refused.\"\n180\t  [space kind ident]\n181\t  (let [as (get-in space [kind ident])]\n182\t    (cond\n183\t      (empty? as) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unknown-image {:yin.k/image ident})\n184\t      (< 1 (count as)) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :ambiguous-image {:yin.k/image ident})\n185\t      :else (segment-of space (first as)))))\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t(defn- inst\n189\t  [seg pc]\n190\t  (nth (:vector seg) pc))\n191\t\n192\t\n193\t(defn- body-of\n194\t  [seg pc]\n195\t  (code/body-index (:bodies seg) pc))\n196\t\n197\t\n198\t(defn phys\n199\t  \"`phys(body(pc), x)`: the physical register R names for virtual `x` in\n200\t   the body holding `pc`.\"\n201\t  [seg pc x]\n202\t  (let [s (get (nth (:phys seg) (body-of seg pc)) x)]\n203\t    (when (nil? s) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :register-layout {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/register x}))\n204\t    s))\n205\t\n206\t\n207\t(defn live-out\n208\t  \"`live-out*(p)`: the union of `L(q)` over p's actual successors (empty\n209\t   for a tail call).\"\n210\t  [seg p]\n211\t  (reduce (fn [acc q] (into acc (analysis/live (:analysis seg) q)))\n212\t          #{}\n213\t          (analysis/successors (:vector seg) p)))\n214\t\n215\t\n216\t(defn register-live\n217\t  \"§5.6 item 3: the `live` operand R must carry at boundary `p`,\n218\t   `(sort (map phys (disj live-out*(p) rd)))`, the destination removed as\n219\t   a virtual id before mapping; `[]` at a tail call.\"\n220\t  [seg p]\n221\t  (vec (sort (map #(phys seg p %) (disj (live-out seg p) (code/rd (inst seg p)))))))\n222\t\n223\t\n224\t(defn virt\n225\t  \"The restricted inverse of `phys` at boundary `p`: the virtual of\n226\t   `live-out*(p)` held in physical `s`. A slot outside that image (only a\n227\t   tampered entry names one) reads as the one virtual of the body R maps\n228\t   there, so the frame validator judges the window; an ambiguous slot is\n229\t   refused.\"\n230\t  [seg p s]\n231\t  (let [m (nth (:phys seg) (body-of seg p))\n232\t        live (filterv #(= s (get m %)) (sort (live-out seg p)))\n233\t        named (filterv #(= s (get m %)) (sort (keys m)))]\n234\t    (cond\n235\t      (= 1 (count live)) (first live)\n236\t      (and (empty? live) (= 1 (count named))) (first named)\n237\t      :else (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :register-layout {:yin.k/pc p :yin.k/register s}))))\n238\t\n239\t\n240\t(defn stack-layout\n241\t  \"§4.3: the virtual registers pushed and not yet consumed while control\n242\t   is inside the expression at A pc `p`, bottom to top.\"\n243\t  [seg p]\n244\t  (get (:layouts seg) p))\n245\t\n246\t\n247\t(defn chain\n248\t  \"The closure pcs owning the body that holds `pc`, outermost first.\"\n249\t  [seg pc]\n250\t  (loop [b (body-of seg pc) out ()]\n251\t    (if-let [owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) b))]\n252\t      (recur (body-of seg owner) (conj out owner))\n253\t      (vec out))))\n254\t\n255\t\n256\t(defn- params\n257\t  [seg c]\n258\t  (nth (inst seg c) 2))\n259\t\n260\t\n261\t(defn env-of\n262\t  \"§4.4 forward: `E` at `pc` from the positional frames `F` (outermost\n263\t   first, values already canonical), the task's free environment and the\n264\t   activation's module store.\"\n265\t  [seg pc free-env frames store-of]\n266\t  (let [cs (chain seg pc)]\n267\t    (when-not (= (count cs) (count frames))\n268\t      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :frame-depth {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/depth (count frames)}))\n269\t    (cond-> (reduce (fn [e [c f]] (merge e (engine/bind-params (params seg c) f)))\n270\t                    (or free-env {})\n271\t                    (map vector cs frames))\n272\t      (some? store-of) (assoc engine/store-of-key store-of))))\n273\t\n274\t\n275\t(defn frames-of\n276\t  \"§4.4 inverse: `F[i] = (mapv #(get E %) params(cᵢ))` over the chain at\n277\t   `pc`. An outer value a shadowing inner binder hides reads as the inner\n278\t   one; the canonical frame never held it.\"\n279\t  [seg pc env]\n280\t  (mapv (fn [c] (mapv #(get env %) (params seg c))) (chain seg pc)))\n281\t\n282\t\n283\t;; =============================================================================\n284\t;; Kernel dispatch\n285\t;; =============================================================================\n286\t\n287\t(defn kernel-kind\n288\t  \"`:stack` or `:register`, by the kernel's link format.\"\n289\t  [k]\n290\t  (let [f (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel k) (:format (module/link-format k)))]\n291\t    (cond\n292\t      (= stack/format-tag f) :stack\n293\t      (= register/format-tag f) :register\n294\t      :else (refuse! :yin.k/unsupported :kernel {:yin.k/format f}))))\n295\t\n296\t\n297\t(defn- image-pc\n298\t  \"`[segment rel-pc]` of absolute kernel pc `pc`.\"\n299\t  [kind k space pc]\n300\t  (let [[ident rel] (or (if (= :stack kind) (stack/image-pc k pc) (register/image-pc k pc))\n301\t                        (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unknown-image {:yin.k/pc pc}))]\n302\t    [(image-segment space kind ident) rel]))\n303\t\n304\t\n305\t(defn offset\n306\t  \"The offset of segment `seg`'s image in kernel `k`'s code space.\"\n307\t  [kind k seg]\n308\t  (let [ident (if (= :stack kind) (:stack-id seg) (:register-id seg))]\n309\t    (or (if (= :stack kind) (stack/absolute-pc k [ident 0]) (register/absolute-pc k [ident 0]))\n310\t        (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied :image-not-attached {:yin.k/segment (:address seg)}))))\n311\t\n312\t\n313\t(def ^:private parking-ops\n314\t  \"A1: the instructions a resume pc may follow, besides a non-tail call.\"\n315\t  #{:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :park :current-continuation})\n316\t\n317\t\n318\t(defn- safepoint!\n319\t  \"Refuse `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` unless the A instruction before `pc`\n320\t   parks (a tail call for a tail state): a layout never invents a\n321\t   safepoint (§4.5).\"\n322\t  [seg pc tail?]\n323\t  (let [t (when (and (integer? pc) (< 0 pc) (<= pc (count (:vector seg)))) (inst seg (dec pc)))\n324\t        op (when t (nth t 0))]\n325\t    (when-not (and t\n326\t                   (= (body-of seg (dec pc)) (body-of seg (min pc (dec (count (:vector seg))))))\n327\t                   (if tail?\n328\t                     (code/tail-call? t)\n329\t                     (or (contains? parking-ops op) (and (= :call op) (not (code/tail-call? t))))))\n330\t      (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc pc}))))\n331\t\n332\t\n333\t(defn- h->a\n334\t  \"The A pc of H pc `hpc`; a `:push` has none and is no safepoint.\"\n335\t  [seg hpc]\n336\t  (or (get (:h->a seg) hpc) (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc hpc})))\n337\t\n338\t\n339\t(defn- a->h\n340\t  [seg pc]\n341\t  (nth (:a->h seg) pc))\n342\t\n343\t\n344\t;; =============================================================================\n345\t;; Values: positional closures and kernel continuations, both ways\n346\t;; =============================================================================\n347\t;;\n348\t;; A lift context `cx` is {:kind :kernel :space :free-env :owner}; a lower\n349\t;; context `lx` adds :address, naming a canonical payload's or closure's\n350\t;; :segment as A.\n351\t\n352\t(declare lift-state lower-state canonical-value positional-value)\n353\t\n354\t\n355\t(defn- walk-value\n356\t  \"`x` with its guest collections rebuilt around `f`, which converts\n357\t   closures and continuations.\"\n358\t  [f x]\n359\t  (cond\n360\t    (values/host-typed? x) (f x)\n361\t    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(walk-value f k) (walk-value f v)])) x)\n362\t    (vector? x) (mapv #(walk-value f %) x)\n363\t    (set? x) (into #{} (map #(walk-value f %)) x)\n364\t    (seq? x) (apply list (map #(walk-value f %) x))\n365\t    :else x))\n366\t\n367\t\n368\t(defn- canonical-closure\n369\t  \"§4.4: a positional closure as the canonical `{:type :closure :params\n370\t   :entry :segment :env}`: `params` from A's `:closure` at the owner of\n371\t   the entry body, `env` by the forward rule over the closure's frames.\"\n372\t  [cx c]\n373\t  (let [[seg rel] (image-pc (:kind cx) (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:body-pc c))\n374\t        entry (if (= :stack (:kind cx)) (h->a seg rel) rel)\n375\t        owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) (body-of seg entry)))\n376\t        _ (when-not (and owner (= entry (nth (inst seg owner) 3)))\n377\t            (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :closure-origin {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n378\t        ps (params seg owner)]\n379\t    (when-not (= (count ps) (:arity c))\n380\t      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :closure-binders {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n381\t    {:type :closure :params ps :entry entry :segment (:address seg)\n382\t     :env (env-of seg owner (:free-env cx)\n383\t                  (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(canonical-value cx %) f)) (:frames c))\n384\t                  (:store-of c))}))\n385\t\n386\t\n387\t(defn- canonical-value*\n388\t  [cx x]\n389\t  (cond\n390\t    (values/closure? x) (values/closure (:owner cx) (canonical-closure cx (values/payload x)))\n391\t    (values/continuation? x)\n392\t    (values/continuation (:owner cx) (assoc (lift-state cx (values/payload x)) :type :reified-continuation))\n393\t    :else x))\n394\t\n395\t\n396\t(defn canonical-value\n397\t  \"Kernel value `x` with every positional closure and kernel continuation\n398\t   reconstructed canonically (cx: a lift context).\"\n399\t  [cx x]\n400\t  (walk-value #(canonical-value* cx %) x))\n401\t\n402\t\n403\t(defn- address-of\n404\t  [lx seg-id]\n405\t  (let [a ((:address lx) seg-id)]\n406\t    (when (nil? a) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg-id}))\n407\t    a))\n408\t\n409\t\n410\t(defn- positional-closure\n411\t  \"The inverse of canonical-closure: the entry's absolute pc in the\n412\t   receiving kernel, the frames read back from `env` by the owner's chain.\"\n413\t  [lx c]\n414\t  (let [seg (segment-of (:space lx) (address-of lx (:segment c)))\n415\t        entry (:entry c)\n416\t        owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) (body-of seg entry)))\n417\t        store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env c))]\n418\t    (when-not (and owner (= entry (nth (inst seg owner) 3)) (= (vec (:params c)) (vec (params seg owner))))\n419\t      (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-binders {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n420\t    (cond-> {:type :closure :arity (count (:params c))\n421\t             :body-pc (+ (offset (:kind lx) (:kernel lx) seg) (if (= :stack (:kind lx)) (a->h seg entry) entry))\n422\t             :frames (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(positional-value lx %) f)) (frames-of seg owner (:env c)))}\n423\t      (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))\n424\t\n425\t\n426\t(defn- positional-value*\n427\t  [lx x]\n428\t  (cond\n429\t    (values/closure? x) (values/closure (:owner lx) (positional-closure lx (values/payload x)))\n430\t    (values/continuation? x)\n431\t    (values/continuation (:owner lx) (merge {:type :reified-continuation} (lower-state lx (values/payload x))))\n432\t    :else x))\n433\t\n434\t\n435\t(defn positional-value\n436\t  \"Canonical value `x` with every closure and continuation lowered into\n437\t   the receiving kernel (lx: a lower context).\"\n438\t  [lx x]\n439\t  (walk-value #(positional-value* lx %) x))\n440\t\n441\t\n442\t;; =============================================================================\n443\t;; Lift: a kernel payload as the canonical act or tail\n444\t;; =============================================================================\n445\t\n446\t(def ^:private kernel-keys\n447\t  \"The register payload keys of either kernel; every other key of an\n448\t   entry is the engine's and travels in the pending.\"\n449\t  #{:segment :site-pc :pc :frames :regs :live :continuation :dest :resume-mode\n450\t    :format :hash :image :images :store-of :stack})\n451\t\n452\t\n453\t(defn- canonical-env\n454\t  [cx seg pc frames store-of]\n455\t  (env-of seg pc (:free-env cx) (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(canonical-value cx %) f)) frames) store-of))\n456\t\n457\t\n458\t(defn- register-window\n459\t  \"§4.2 step 4: `{virt(site, s) V}` over the entry's `[s V]` pairs.\"\n460\t  [cx seg site regs]\n461\t  (into {} (map (fn [[s x]] [(virt seg site s) (canonical-value cx x)])) regs))\n462\t\n463\t\n464\t(defn- register-kframe\n465\t  \"§4.2 step 6, one frame independently: its own image row and A, `rd`\n466\t   from A, never the physical `:dest`.\"\n467\t  [cx f]\n468\t  (let [[seg pc] (image-pc :register (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:return-pc f))]\n469\t    (safepoint! seg pc false)\n470\t    {:type :return :segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n471\t     :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames f) (:store-of f))\n472\t     :window (register-window cx seg (dec pc) (:regs f))\n473\t     :rd (code/rd (inst seg (dec pc)))}))\n474\t\n475\t\n476\t(defn- lift-register\n477\t  [cx entry]\n478\t  (let [[seg pc] (image-pc :register (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:pc entry))\n479\t        tail? (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\n480\t        _ (safepoint! seg pc tail?)\n481\t        k (mapv #(register-kframe cx %) (:continuation entry))]\n482\t    (if tail?\n483\t      {:segment (:address seg) :site (dec pc) :k k :deliver {:deliver :return}}\n484\t      {:segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n485\t       :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames entry) (:store-of entry))\n486\t       :window (register-window cx seg (dec pc) (:regs entry))\n487\t       :k k\n488\t       :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd (code/rd (inst seg (dec pc)))}})))\n489\t\n490\t\n491\t(defn slices\n492\t  \"§4.3's K slices of operand stack `st` under return frames whose bases\n493\t   are `bases`, outermost first: `St[b(i-1), b(i))` per frame with\n494\t   `b(-1) = 0`, then the current activation's `St[b(m-1), n)`.\"\n495\t  [st bases]\n496\t  (let [bounds (into [0] bases)]\n497\t    (conj (mapv (fn [lo hi] (subvec st lo hi)) bounds (rest bounds))\n498\t          (subvec st (peek bounds) (count st)))))\n499\t\n500\t\n501\t(defn- slice-window\n502\t  \"`(zipmap (stack-layout (dec pc)) slice)`; the two have equal length.\"\n503\t  [cx seg pc slice]\n504\t  (let [layout (stack-layout seg (dec pc))]\n505\t    (when-not (= (count layout) (count slice))\n506\t      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :stack-layout {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/layout layout :yin.k/slice (count slice)}))\n507\t    (zipmap layout (map #(canonical-value cx %) slice))))\n508\t\n509\t\n510\t(defn- stack-site\n511\t  \"`[segment site]`: the A pc of the parking instruction before absolute\n512\t   stack resume pc `abs`.\"\n513\t  [cx abs]\n514\t  (let [[seg rel] (image-pc :stack (:kernel cx) (:space cx) abs)]\n515\t    [seg (h->a seg (dec rel))]))\n516\t\n517\t\n518\t(defn- lift-stack\n519\t  [cx entry]\n520\t  (let [st (vec (:stack entry))\n521\t        frames (vec (:continuation entry))\n522\t        bases (mapv :stack-base frames)\n523\t        _ (when-not (and (every? integer? bases) (apply <= 0 (conj bases (count st))))\n524\t            (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :stack-base {:yin.k/bases bases}))\n525\t        parts (slices st bases)\n526\t        [seg site] (stack-site cx (:pc entry))\n527\t        tail? (code/tail-call? (inst seg site))\n528\t        _ (safepoint! seg (inc site) tail?)\n529\t        k (mapv (fn [f slice]\n530\t                  (let [[fseg fsite] (stack-site cx (:return-pc f))\n531\t                        pc (inc fsite)]\n532\t                    (safepoint! fseg pc false)\n533\t                    {:type :return :segment (:address fseg) :pc pc\n534\t                     :env (canonical-env cx fseg pc (:frames f) (:store-of f))\n535\t                     :window (slice-window cx fseg pc slice)\n536\t                     :rd (code/rd (inst fseg fsite))}))\n537\t                frames parts)]\n538\t    (if tail?\n539\t      ;; frozen §2.4: the current frames, store-of and slice are dead\n540\t      {:segment (:address seg) :site site :k k :deliver {:deliver :return}}\n541\t      (let [pc (inc site)]\n542\t        {:segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n543\t         :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames entry) (:store-of entry))\n544\t         :window (slice-window cx seg pc (peek parts))\n545\t         :k k\n546\t         :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd (code/rd (inst seg site))}}))))\n547\t\n548\t\n549\t(defn lift-state\n550\t  \"A kernel's wait entry, parked record or reified payload as the\n551\t   canonical act or tail payload (§4.2, §4.3), engine fields carried.\"\n552\t  [cx entry]\n553\t  (let [fields (apply dissoc entry kernel-keys)]\n554\t    (merge (cond-> fields (contains? fields :datom) (update :datom #(canonical-value cx %)))\n555\t           (if (= :stack (:kind cx)) (lift-stack cx entry) (lift-register cx entry)))))\n556\t\n557\t\n558\t(defn lift-context\n559\t  \"The lift context of kernel `k` over `space`; positional closures and\n560\t   kernel continuations are reminted under `owner`.\"\n561\t  [k space owner]\n562\t  (assoc {} :kind (kernel-kind k) :kernel k :space space :free-env (or (:free-env k) {}) :owner owner))\n563\t\n564\t\n565\t;; =============================================================================\n566\t;; Lower: a canonical act or tail into a kernel\n567\t;; =============================================================================\n568\t\n569\t(defn- lower-frames\n570\t  [lx seg pc env]\n571\t  (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(positional-value lx %) f)) (frames-of seg pc env)))\n572\t\n573\t\n574\t(defn- payload-segment\n575\t  [lx p]\n576\t  (segment-of (:space lx) (address-of lx (:segment p))))\n577\t\n578\t\n579\t(defn- lower-regs\n580\t  \"`(sort-by first [[phys(v) V] …])` over window `w`.\"\n581\t  [lx seg site w]\n582\t  (vec (sort-by first (map (fn [[x v]] [(phys seg site x) (positional-value lx v)]) w))))\n583\t\n584\t\n585\t(defn- register-k\n586\t  [lx k]\n587\t  (mapv (fn [f]\n588\t          (let [seg (payload-segment lx f)\n589\t                off (offset :register (:kernel lx) seg)\n590\t                pc (:pc f)\n591\t                regs (lower-regs lx seg (dec pc) (:window f))\n592\t                store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env f))]\n593\t            (cond-> {:site-pc (+ off pc -1) :return-pc (+ off pc)\n594\t                     :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env f))\n595\t                     :regs regs :live (mapv first regs)\n596\t                     :dest (phys seg (dec pc) (:rd f))}\n597\t              (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))\n598\t        k))\n599\t\n600\t\n601\t(defn- lower-register\n602\t  [lx p fill]\n603\t  (let [k (:kernel lx)\n604\t        seg (payload-segment lx p)\n605\t        off (offset :register k seg)\n606\t        common (cond-> {:segment (:segment k) :format register/format-tag :hash (:hash k)\n607\t                        :image (:register-id seg) :continuation (register-k lx (:k p))}\n608\t                 (< 1 (count (:images k))) (assoc :images (:images k)))]\n609\t    (if (contains? p :site)\n610\t      (cond-> (merge common {:site-pc (+ off (:site p)) :pc (+ off (:site p) 1)\n611\t                             :frames (get fill :frames []) :regs [] :live [] :dest nil\n612\t                             :resume-mode :return-result})\n613\t        (some? (:store-of fill)) (assoc :store-of (:store-of fill)))\n614\t      (let [pc (:pc p)\n615\t            regs (lower-regs lx seg (dec pc) (:window p))\n616\t            store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env p))]\n617\t        (cond-> (merge common {:site-pc (+ off pc -1) :pc (+ off pc)\n618\t                               :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env p))\n619\t                               :regs regs :live (mapv first regs)\n620\t                               :dest (phys seg (dec pc) (get-in p [:deliver :rd]))\n621\t                               :resume-mode :write-result})\n622\t          (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n623\t\n624\t\n625\t(defn- layout-slice\n626\t  \"`(mapv W (stack-layout (dec pc)))`, every member present in W.\"\n627\t  [lx seg pc w]\n628\t  (mapv (fn [x]\n629\t          (when-not (contains? w x)\n630\t            (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable :window-missing {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/register x}))\n631\t          (positional-value lx (get w x)))\n632\t        (stack-layout seg (dec pc))))\n633\t\n634\t\n635\t(defn- stack-k\n636\t  \"`[frames stack]`: each return frame's slice appended in order, its base\n637\t   the cumulative length through its own slice (§4.3), `b(i) = b(i-1) +\n638\t   |slice(i)|`.\"\n639\t  [lx k]\n640\t  (reduce (fn [[frames st] f]\n641\t            (let [seg (payload-segment lx f)\n642\t                  pc (:pc f)\n643\t                  st (into st (layout-slice lx seg pc (:window f)))\n644\t                  store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env f))]\n645\t              [(conj frames (cond-> {:return-pc (+ (offset :stack (:kernel lx) seg) (a->h seg (dec pc)) 1)\n646\t                                     :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env f))\n647\t                                     :stack-base (count st)}\n648\t                              (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of)))\n649\t               st]))\n650\t          [[] []]\n651\t          k))\n652\t\n653\t\n654\t(defn- lower-stack\n655\t  [lx p fill]\n656\t  (let [k (:kernel lx)\n657\t        seg (payload-segment lx p)\n658\t        off (offset :stack k seg)\n659\t        [frames st] (stack-k lx (:k p))\n660\t        common {:segment (:segment k) :format stack/format-tag :hash (:hash k) :image (:stack-id seg)\n661\t                :continuation frames}]\n662\t    (if (contains? p :site)\n663\t      (cond-> (merge common {:pc (+ off (a->h seg (:site p)) 1) :resume-mode :return-result\n664\t                             :stack st :frames (get fill :frames [])})\n665\t        (some? (:store-of fill)) (assoc :store-of (:store-of fill)))\n666\t      (let [pc (:pc p)\n667\t            store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env p))]\n668\t        (cond-> (merge common {:pc (+ off (a->h seg (dec pc)) 1)\n669\t                               :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env p))\n670\t                               :stack (into st (layout-slice lx seg pc (:window p)))})\n671\t          (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n672\t\n673\t\n674\t(def ^:private canonical-keys\n675\t  #{:segment :pc :site :env :window :k :deliver :type :id})\n676\t\n677\t\n678\t(defn lower-state\n679\t  \"Canonical act or tail payload `p` as the receiving kernel's entry\n680\t   (§4.2, §4.3), engine fields carried. `fill` gives a lowered tail's\n681\t   `:frames`/`:store-of` (default `[]`/nil), which the return transition\n682\t   replaces unread (§5.6 item 8).\"\n683\t  ([lx p] (lower-state lx p {}))\n684\t  ([lx p fill]\n685\t   (let [fields (apply dissoc p canonical-keys)]\n686\t     (merge (cond-> fields (contains? fields :datom) (update :datom #(positional-value lx %)))\n687\t            (if (= :stack (:kind lx)) (lower-stack lx p fill) (lower-register lx p fill))))))\n688\t\n689\t\n690\t(defn lower-context\n691\t  \"The lower context into kernel `k` over `space`; `address` maps a\n692\t   payload's or closure's `:segment` to A (default: it is A).\"\n693\t  ([k space] (lower-context k space identity))\n694\t  ([k space address]\n695\t   (assoc {} :kind (kernel-kind k) :kernel k :space space :free-env (or (:free-env k) {})\n696\t          :owner (:owner k) :address address)))\n697\t\n698\t\n699\t;; =============================================================================\n700\t;; Tasks\n701\t;; =============================================================================\n702\t\n703\t(defn canonical-task\n704\t  \"Quiescent kernel `k` presented as semantic-register machine `template`\n705\t   (a fresh machine of the same composition) for `rows/lift-task`: code\n706\t   by A from `space`, every wait, parked record and value reconstructed\n707\t   through the layout; resources, stores and counters carried. A running\n708\t   kernel is `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; install children are not carried\n709\t   by this phase's layouts.\"\n710\t  [k space template]\n711\t  (when (engine/active-continuation? k)\n712\t    (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc (:pc k)}))\n713\t  (when (seq (:installs k))\n714\t    (refuse! :yin.k/unsupported :installs {:yin.k/names (vec (keys (:installs k)))}))\n715\t  (let [cx (lift-context k space (:owner template))\n716\t        conv #(canonical-value cx %)\n717\t        parked (into {} (map (fn [[id rec]] [id (assoc (lift-state cx rec) :type :parked-continuation :id id)]))\n718\t                     (:parked k))\n719\t        value (:value k)\n720\t        parked-value? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? parked (:id value)))\n721\t        code (into {} (map (fn [[a s]] [a (assoc {} :vector (:vector s) :address a :analysis (:analysis s))]))\n722\t                   (:segments space))]\n723\t    (assoc template\n724\t           :code code\n725\t           :code-aliases (into {} (map (fn [a] [a a])) (keys code))\n726\t           :program nil :control nil :window {} :k nil\n727\t           :resources (:resources k)\n728\t           :capability-secret (:capability-secret k)\n729\t           :free-env (:free-env k)\n730\t           :env (or (:free-env k) {})\n731\t           :store (conv (:store k))\n732\t           :module-stores (conv (or (:module-stores k) {}))\n733\t           :parked parked\n734\t           :wait-set (mapv #(lift-state cx %) (:wait-set k))\n735\t           :ready-queue (:ready-queue k)\n736\t           :value (if parked-value? (get parked (:id value)) (conv value))\n737\t           :id-counter (:id-counter k)\n738\t           :installs {}\n739\t           :halted? (:halted? k)\n740\t           :blocked? (:blocked? k))))\n741\t\n742\t\n743\t(defn lift-task\n744\t  \"§7.1 for a de Bruijn kernel: `rows/lift-task` over its canonical\n745\t   presentation. `template` is a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n746\t   kernel's composition; opts as rows/lift-task's.\"\n747\t  [k space template serve! opts]\n748\t  (rows/lift-task (canonical-task k space template) serve! opts))\n749\t\n750\t\n751\t(defn attach-space\n752\t  \"Kernel `k` holding the derived image of every segment of `space`, in\n753\t   A order (§7.2: derive and attach the image for each A).\"\n754\t  [k space]\n755\t  (let [kind (kernel-kind k)]\n756\t    (reduce (fn [k a]\n757\t              (let [seg (segment-of space a)]\n758\t                (if (= :stack kind)\n759\t                  (stack/attach-image k (:stack seg) vm/stack-contract)\n760\t                  (register/attach-image k (:register seg) vm/register-contract))))\n761\t            k\n762\t            (sort-by str (keys (:segments space))))))\n763\t\n764\t\n765\t(defn machine-space\n766\t  \"The space of the A vectors semantic-register machine `m` holds, and\n767\t   the map from its segment ids to A.\"\n768\t  [m]\n769\t  [(space (map :vector (vals (:code m))))\n770\t   (fn [seg] (or (get-in m [:code seg :address]) (when (contains? (:code-aliases m) seg) seg)))])\n771\t\n772\t\n773\t(defn kernel-task\n774\t  \"Step 12 for a de Bruijn receiver: semantic-register machine `m` (what\n775\t   `rows/lower-task` restored) as fresh kernel `k` of the same\n776\t   composition: every image derived and attached, the free environment\n777\t   set, every wait, parked record and value lowered through the layout.\n778\t   Delivers nothing, runs nothing.\"\n779\t  [m k]\n780\t  (let [[sp address] (machine-space m)\n781\t        k (attach-space k sp)\n782\t        lx (lower-context k sp address)\n783\t        conv #(positional-value lx %)\n784\t        parked (into {} (map (fn [[id rec]] [id (assoc (lower-state lx rec) :type :parked-continuation :id id)]))\n785\t                     (:parked m))\n786\t        value (:value m)\n787\t        parked-value? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? parked (:id value)))]\n788\t    (assoc k\n789\t           :resources (:resources m)\n790\t           :free-env (:free-env m)\n791\t           :store (conv (:store m))\n792\t           :module-stores (conv (or (:module-stores m) {}))\n793\t           :parked parked\n794\t           :wait-set (mapv #(lower-state lx %) (:wait-set m))\n795\t           :ready-queue []\n796\t           :value (if parked-value? (get parked (:id value)) (conv value))\n797\t           :id-counter (:id-counter m)\n798\t           :halted? (:halted? m)\n799\t           :blocked? (:blocked? m))))\n800\t\n801\t\n802\t(defn- lexical-names\n803\t  \"The names the chain binds at `pc` of `v`.\"\n804\t  [v pc]\n805\t  (let [bodies (code/body-ranges v)]\n806\t    (loop [b (code/body-index bodies pc) out #{}]\n807\t      (if-let [owner (:owner (nth bodies b))]\n808\t        (recur (code/body-index bodies owner) (into out (nth (nth v owner) 2)))\n809\t        out))))\n810\t\n811\t\n812\t(declare state-prim)\n813\t\n814\t\n815\t(defn- value-prim\n816\t  \"The path to the first `:prim` row carrier value `x` reaches as kernel\n817\t   payload data: through guest collections, a closure's lexical bindings\n818\t   (its positional frames) and a capture's state; or nil.\"\n819\t  [code x path]\n820\t  (when (and (vector? x) (= :row (first x)))\n821\t    (let [n (second x) ss (:slots n)]\n822\t      (case (:kind n)\n823\t        :prim path\n824\t        (:vec :list :set :map) (some (fn [[i y]] (value-prim code y (conj path i))) (map-indexed vector ss))\n825\t        :closure (let [[a entry _ bindings] ss\n826\t                       v (get code a)\n827\t                       owner (when v (some (fn [pc]\n828\t                                             (let [t (nth v pc)]\n829\t                                               (when (and (= :closure (nth t 0)) (= entry (nth t 3))) pc)))\n830\t                                           (range (count v))))\n831\t                       names (if owner (lexical-names v owner) #{})]\n832\t                   (some (fn [[s y]] (when (contains? names s) (value-prim code y (conj path s))))\n833\t                         (partition 2 (:slots bindings))))\n834\t        :reified (state-prim code (first ss) (conj path 0))\n835\t        nil))))\n836\t\n837\t\n838\t(defn- frame-prim\n839\t  \"A frame's window and lexical bindings (§4.4: the free part is the\n840\t   kernel's :free-env, never payload data).\"\n841\t  [code a pc e w path]\n842\t  (let [names (lexical-names (get code a) pc)]\n843\t    (or (some (fn [[r y]] (value-prim code y (conj path :window r))) (partition 2 (:slots w)))\n844\t        (some (fn [[sym y]] (when (contains? names sym) (value-prim code y (conj path :env sym))))\n845\t              (partition 2 (:slots (first (:slots e))))))))\n846\t\n847\t\n848\t(defn- state-prim\n849\t  [code n path]\n850\t  (let [kframes (fn [k]\n851\t                  (some (fn [[i f]]\n852\t                          (let [[a pc e w] (:slots f)]\n853\t                            (frame-prim code a pc e w (conj path :k i))))\n854\t                        (map-indexed vector (:slots k))))\n855\t        [a pc e w k] (:slots n)]\n856\t    (case (:kind n)\n857\t      :act (or (frame-prim code a pc e w path) (kframes k))\n858\t      :tail (kframes e)\n859\t      nil)))\n860\t\n861\t\n862\t(defn lower-defect\n863\t  \"What a kernel of `kind` cannot hold, judged on decoded task `task`\n864\t   before anything is attached: install children (not carried by this\n865\t   phase's layouts), and for the register kernel a primitive function in\n866\t   the payload data of a wait or parked state (a window, a lexical\n867\t   binding, or reached through them), which its restore refuses as\n868\t   `:continuation-registers` (`vm/machine-data?`). nil when it can.\"\n869\t  [task kind]\n870\t  (let [slots (:slots task)\n871\t        code (nth slots 11)]\n872\t    (cond\n873\t      (seq (nth slots 12))\n874\t      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :installs)\n875\t\n876\t      (= :register kind)\n877\t      (when-let [path (or (some (fn [[i w]] (state-prim code (first (:slots w)) [:frames i]))\n878\t                                (map-indexed vector (nth slots 13)))\n879\t                          (some (fn [[p st]] (state-prim code st [:parked p]))\n880\t                                (partition 2 (:slots (nth slots 8)))))]\n881\t        (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :continuation-registers :yin.k/path path))\n882\t\n883\t      :else nil)))\n884\t\n885\t\n886\t(defn lower-task\n887\t  \"§7.2 into a de Bruijn kernel: decode `wire`, refuse what kernel `k`\n888\t   cannot hold (`lower-defect`) before any attach, then `rows/lower-task`\n889\t   into `scratch` (a fresh semantic-register machine of the same\n890\t   composition: the carrier's steps 1-11 and restore) and `kernel-task`\n891\t   into `k`. Throws the first refusal as ex-data.\"\n892\t  ([scratch k wire attach!] (lower-task scratch k wire attach! {}))\n893\t  ([scratch k wire attach! opts]\n894\t   (let [task (rows/decode wire (merge rows/default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n895\t     (when (= :task (:kind task))\n896\t       (when-let [d (lower-defect task (kernel-kind k))]\n897\t         (throw (ex-info \"Layout refused\" d))))\n898\t     (kernel-task (rows/lower-task scratch wire attach! opts) k))))\n899\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da6a8ed-da80-4f95-b938-953b362e5554","uuid":"6d260a2f-8867-4a08-acab-085834ba00a0","timestamp":"2026-10-12T18:26:16.496Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.layout\n  \"Phase 6c (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §4):\n   the de Bruijn register and stack kernels reconstruct the canonical\n   frame of the register machine through their layouts, and lower it\n   back.\n\n   Static half, per segment A: `segment` derives R(A) and H(A) and reads\n   off the register pairing (`phys`, the restricted inverse `virt`, the\n   kernel's `live` as live-out with tail boundaries `[]`), the stack\n   correspondence (`h->a`, `a->h`, every `:push` removed) and the operand\n   layout `stack-layout` (the values pushed and not yet consumed while\n   control is inside a pc's expression). A `space` indexes segments by\n   the kernels' image identities, R and H, which are checksums: A is the\n   only code identity.\n\n   Dynamic half: `lift-state` reads a kernel's wait entry, parked record\n   or reified payload as the canonical `act` or `tail` payload the\n   semantic-register evaluator mints (`{:segment A :pc :env :window :k\n   :deliver}`, `{:segment A :site :k :deliver}`, engine fields carried);\n   `lower-state` is its inverse. The register kernel's return\n   destinations are recovered from A, never from the physical `:dest`;\n   the stack kernel's operand stack is sliced `[previous-base, base)` per\n   frame and lowered with cumulative bases. `E` is the free environment\n   merged under the chain's positional frames (§4.4); the inverse reads\n   each frame back from `E` by the chain, never the free environment.\n\n   Task level: `canonical-task` presents a quiescent kernel as a\n   semantic-register machine for `yin.vm.ucf.rows/lift-task`;\n   `kernel-task` restores a machine `rows/lower-task` produced into a\n   fresh kernel; `lift-task` and `lower-task` compose them with the row\n   carrier, the lower refusing what a kernel cannot hold before any\n   stream is attached. A layout never runs code, never fills a binding\n   from the receiver and never invents a safepoint (§4.5).\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as register]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as stack]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.derive :as derive]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n(defn- refuse!\n  [status kind data]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Layout refused\" (merge data (assoc {} :yin.k/status status :yin.k/kind kind)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Static half: one segment\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- operands\n  \"The register operands of an A tuple, destination first, then its uses\n   in table order.\"\n  [t]\n  (into (if-some [r (code/rd t)] [r] []) (code/uses t)))\n\n\n(defn- register-operands\n  \"The `:reg`/`:regs` operands of an R tuple in table order (the `:live`\n   slot is `:data`, never paired).\"\n  [t]\n  (into []\n        (mapcat (fn [[[_ kind] x]] (case kind :reg [x] :regs x [])))\n        (map vector (get rcode/opcode-table (nth t 0)) (rest t))))\n\n\n(defn register-pairs\n  \"`[pc virtual physical]` for every register operand of every pc: A's\n   tuple and R's name their registers in the same slots (phase-5 §2.4).\"\n  [v image]\n  (into []\n        (mapcat (fn [pc]\n                  (map (fn [x s] [pc x s])\n                       (operands (nth v pc))\n                       (register-operands (nth (:instructions image) pc)))))\n        (range (count v))))\n\n\n(defn- phys-maps\n  \"Per body, `{virtual physical}` read off the pairs; the first pc that\n   names a virtual wins (register-pairing checks they agree).\"\n  [bodies pairs]\n  (reduce (fn [acc [pc x s]]\n            (let [b (code/body-index bodies pc)]\n              (if (contains? (nth acc b) x) acc (assoc-in acc [b x] s))))\n          (vec (repeat (count bodies) {}))\n          pairs))\n\n\n(defn correspondence\n  \"§4.3 static item 1: H with every `:push` removed corresponds one to one,\n   in order, with A. Answers `{:a->h [h-pc …] :h->a {h-pc a-pc}}`.\"\n  [h]\n  (reduce (fn [acc hpc]\n            (if (= :push (nth (nth h hpc) 0))\n              acc\n              (-> acc\n                  (update :a->h conj hpc)\n                  (assoc-in [:h->a hpc] (count (:a->h acc))))))\n          {:a->h [] :h->a {}}\n          (range (count h))))\n\n\n(def ^:private pushing-ops\n  \"The parse nodes whose children before the current one are pushed:\n   `:call` (the operator and earlier operands), `:ffi-call` (earlier\n   operands) and `:stream-put` (the target, while the value runs).\"\n  #{:call :ffi-call :stream-put})\n\n\n(defn- stack-layouts\n  \"§4.3 static item 2 for every pc of every body: `{pc [virtual …]}`,\n   bottom to top, over the parse tree's ancestors outermost first.\"\n  [v bodies]\n  (letfn [(walk\n            [out node pending]\n            (let [out (assoc out (:pc node) pending)\n                  pushes? (contains? pushing-ops (:op node))\n                  uses (when pushes? (code/uses (nth v (:pc node))))]\n              (reduce (fn [out [i child]]\n                        (walk out child (if pushes? (into pending (take i uses)) pending)))\n                      out\n                      (map-indexed vector (:children node)))))]\n    (reduce (fn [out body] (walk out (:expr body) [])) {} bodies)))\n\n\n(defn segment\n  \"The static facts of one admitted A vector `v`, for both kernels.\"\n  [v]\n  (let [bodies (code/parse v)\n        r (derive/register-image v)\n        h (:image (derive/stack-image v))\n        pairs (register-pairs v r)]\n    (merge {:vector v\n            :address (jing/segment-key v)\n            :bodies bodies\n            :analysis (analysis/analyze v)\n            :register r\n            :register-id (rcode/register-hash r)\n            :stack h\n            :stack-id (dcode/image-hash h)\n            :pairs pairs\n            :phys (phys-maps bodies pairs)\n            :layouts (stack-layouts v bodies)}\n           (correspondence h))))\n\n\n(defn space\n  \"Segments by A, and A by each kernel's image identity. `segments` is a\n   seq of `segment` results or of A vectors.\"\n  [segments]\n  (reduce (fn [acc s]\n            (let [s (if (map? s) s (segment s))\n                  a (:address s)]\n              (-> acc\n                  (assoc-in [:segments a] s)\n                  (update-in [:register (:register-id s)] (fnil conj #{}) a)\n                  (update-in [:stack (:stack-id s)] (fnil conj #{}) a))))\n          {:segments {} :register {} :stack {}}\n          segments))\n\n\n(defn segment-of\n  \"The segment A names in `space`.\"\n  [space a]\n  (or (get-in space [:segments a])\n      (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied :segment {:yin.k/segment a})))\n\n\n(defn- image-segment\n  \"The segment whose `kind` image is `ident`: an identity is a checksum,\n   so two A deriving one image are ambiguous and refused.\"\n  [space kind ident]\n  (let [as (get-in space [kind ident])]\n    (cond\n      (empty? as) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unknown-image {:yin.k/image ident})\n      (< 1 (count as)) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :ambiguous-image {:yin.k/image ident})\n      :else (segment-of space (first as)))))\n\n\n(defn- inst\n  [seg pc]\n  (nth (:vector seg) pc))\n\n\n(defn- body-of\n  [seg pc]\n  (code/body-index (:bodies seg) pc))\n\n\n(defn phys\n  \"`phys(body(pc), x)`: the physical register R names for virtual `x` in\n   the body holding `pc`.\"\n  [seg pc x]\n  (let [s (get (nth (:phys seg) (body-of seg pc)) x)]\n    (when (nil? s) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :register-layout {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/register x}))\n    s))\n\n\n(defn live-out\n  \"`live-out*(p)`: the union of `L(q)` over p's actual successors (empty\n   for a tail call).\"\n  [seg p]\n  (reduce (fn [acc q] (into acc (analysis/live (:analysis seg) q)))\n          #{}\n          (analysis/successors (:vector seg) p)))\n\n\n(defn register-live\n  \"§5.6 item 3: the `live` operand R must carry at boundary `p`,\n   `(sort (map phys (disj live-out*(p) rd)))`, the destination removed as\n   a virtual id before mapping; `[]` at a tail call.\"\n  [seg p]\n  (vec (sort (map #(phys seg p %) (disj (live-out seg p) (code/rd (inst seg p)))))))\n\n\n(defn virt\n  \"The restricted inverse of `phys` at boundary `p`: the virtual of\n   `live-out*(p)` held in physical `s`. A slot outside that image (only a\n   tampered entry names one) reads as the one virtual of the body R maps\n   there, so the frame validator judges the window; an ambiguous slot is\n   refused.\"\n  [seg p s]\n  (let [m (nth (:phys seg) (body-of seg p))\n        live (filterv #(= s (get m %)) (sort (live-out seg p)))\n        named (filterv #(= s (get m %)) (sort (keys m)))]\n    (cond\n      (= 1 (count live)) (first live)\n      (and (empty? live) (= 1 (count named))) (first named)\n      :else (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :register-layout {:yin.k/pc p :yin.k/register s}))))\n\n\n(defn stack-layout\n  \"§4.3: the virtual registers pushed and not yet consumed while control\n   is inside the expression at A pc `p`, bottom to top.\"\n  [seg p]\n  (get (:layouts seg) p))\n\n\n(defn chain\n  \"The closure pcs owning the body that holds `pc`, outermost first.\"\n  [seg pc]\n  (loop [b (body-of seg pc) out ()]\n    (if-let [owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) b))]\n      (recur (body-of seg owner) (conj out owner))\n      (vec out))))\n\n\n(defn- params\n  [seg c]\n  (nth (inst seg c) 2))\n\n\n(defn env-of\n  \"§4.4 forward: `E` at `pc` from the positional frames `F` (outermost\n   first, values already canonical), the task's free environment and the\n   activation's module store.\"\n  [seg pc free-env frames store-of]\n  (let [cs (chain seg pc)]\n    (when-not (= (count cs) (count frames))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :frame-depth {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/depth (count frames)}))\n    (cond-> (reduce (fn [e [c f]] (merge e (engine/bind-params (params seg c) f)))\n                    (or free-env {})\n                    (map vector cs frames))\n      (some? store-of) (assoc engine/store-of-key store-of))))\n\n\n(defn frames-of\n  \"§4.4 inverse: `F[i] = (mapv #(get E %) params(cᵢ))` over the chain at\n   `pc`. An outer value a shadowing inner binder hides reads as the inner\n   one; the canonical frame never held it.\"\n  [seg pc env]\n  (mapv (fn [c] (mapv #(get env %) (params seg c))) (chain seg pc)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Kernel dispatch\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn kernel-kind\n  \"`:stack` or `:register`, by the kernel's link format.\"\n  [k]\n  (let [f (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel k) (:format (module/link-format k)))]\n    (cond\n      (= stack/format-tag f) :stack\n      (= register/format-tag f) :register\n      :else (refuse! :yin.k/unsupported :kernel {:yin.k/format f}))))\n\n\n(defn- image-pc\n  \"`[segment rel-pc]` of absolute kernel pc `pc`.\"\n  [kind k space pc]\n  (let [[ident rel] (or (if (= :stack kind) (stack/image-pc k pc) (register/image-pc k pc))\n                        (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unknown-image {:yin.k/pc pc}))]\n    [(image-segment space kind ident) rel]))\n\n\n(defn offset\n  \"The offset of segment `seg`'s image in kernel `k`'s code space.\"\n  [kind k seg]\n  (let [ident (if (= :stack kind) (:stack-id seg) (:register-id seg))]\n    (or (if (= :stack kind) (stack/absolute-pc k [ident 0]) (register/absolute-pc k [ident 0]))\n        (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied :image-not-attached {:yin.k/segment (:address seg)}))))\n\n\n(def ^:private parking-ops\n  \"A1: the instructions a resume pc may follow, besides a non-tail call.\"\n  #{:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :park :current-continuation})\n\n\n(defn- safepoint!\n  \"Refuse `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` unless the A instruction before `pc`\n   parks (a tail call for a tail state): a layout never invents a\n   safepoint (§4.5).\"\n  [seg pc tail?]\n  (let [t (when (and (integer? pc) (< 0 pc) (<= pc (count (:vector seg)))) (inst seg (dec pc)))\n        op (when t (nth t 0))]\n    (when-not (and t\n                   (= (body-of seg (dec pc)) (body-of seg (min pc (dec (count (:vector seg))))))\n                   (if tail?\n                     (code/tail-call? t)\n                     (or (contains? parking-ops op) (and (= :call op) (not (code/tail-call? t))))))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc pc}))))\n\n\n(defn- h->a\n  \"The A pc of H pc `hpc`; a `:push` has none and is no safepoint.\"\n  [seg hpc]\n  (or (get (:h->a seg) hpc) (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc hpc})))\n\n\n(defn- a->h\n  [seg pc]\n  (nth (:a->h seg) pc))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Values: positional closures and kernel continuations, both ways\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; A lift context `cx` is {:kind :kernel :space :free-env :owner}; a lower\n;; context `lx` adds :address, naming a canonical payload's or closure's\n;; :segment as A.\n\n(declare lift-state lower-state canonical-value positional-value)\n\n\n(defn- walk-value\n  \"`x` with its guest collections rebuilt around `f`, which converts\n   closures and continuations.\"\n  [f x]\n  (cond\n    (values/host-typed? x) (f x)\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(walk-value f k) (walk-value f v)])) x)\n    (vector? x) (mapv #(walk-value f %) x)\n    (set? x) (into #{} (map #(walk-value f %)) x)\n    (seq? x) (apply list (map #(walk-value f %) x))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn- canonical-closure\n  \"§4.4: a positional closure as the canonical `{:type :closure :params\n   :entry :segment :env}`: `params` from A's `:closure` at the owner of\n   the entry body, `env` by the forward rule over the closure's frames.\"\n  [cx c]\n  (let [[seg rel] (image-pc (:kind cx) (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:body-pc c))\n        entry (if (= :stack (:kind cx)) (h->a seg rel) rel)\n        owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) (body-of seg entry)))\n        _ (when-not (and owner (= entry (nth (inst seg owner) 3)))\n            (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :closure-origin {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n        ps (params seg owner)]\n    (when-not (= (count ps) (:arity c))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :closure-binders {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n    {:type :closure :params ps :entry entry :segment (:address seg)\n     :env (env-of seg owner (:free-env cx)\n                  (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(canonical-value cx %) f)) (:frames c))\n                  (:store-of c))}))\n\n\n(defn- canonical-value*\n  [cx x]\n  (cond\n    (values/closure? x) (values/closure (:owner cx) (canonical-closure cx (values/payload x)))\n    (values/continuation? x)\n    (values/continuation (:owner cx) (assoc (lift-state cx (values/payload x)) :type :reified-continuation))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn canonical-value\n  \"Kernel value `x` with every positional closure and kernel continuation\n   reconstructed canonically (cx: a lift context).\"\n  [cx x]\n  (walk-value #(canonical-value* cx %) x))\n\n\n(defn- address-of\n  [lx seg-id]\n  (let [a ((:address lx) seg-id)]\n    (when (nil? a) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg-id}))\n    a))\n\n\n(defn- positional-closure\n  \"The inverse of canonical-closure: the entry's absolute pc in the\n   receiving kernel, the frames read back from `env` by the owner's chain.\"\n  [lx c]\n  (let [seg (segment-of (:space lx) (address-of lx (:segment c)))\n        entry (:entry c)\n        owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) (body-of seg entry)))\n        store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env c))]\n    (when-not (and owner (= entry (nth (inst seg owner) 3)) (= (vec (:params c)) (vec (params seg owner))))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-binders {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n    (cond-> {:type :closure :arity (count (:params c))\n             :body-pc (+ (offset (:kind lx) (:kernel lx) seg) (if (= :stack (:kind lx)) (a->h seg entry) entry))\n             :frames (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(positional-value lx %) f)) (frames-of seg owner (:env c)))}\n      (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))\n\n\n(defn- positional-value*\n  [lx x]\n  (cond\n    (values/closure? x) (values/closure (:owner lx) (positional-closure lx (values/payload x)))\n    (values/continuation? x)\n    (values/continuation (:owner lx) (merge {:type :reified-continuation} (lower-state lx (values/payload x))))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn positional-value\n  \"Canonical value `x` with every closure and continuation lowered into\n   the receiving kernel (lx: a lower context).\"\n  [lx x]\n  (walk-value #(positional-value* lx %) x))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Lift: a kernel payload as the canonical act or tail\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private kernel-keys\n  \"The register payload keys of either kernel; every other key of an\n   entry is the engine's and travels in the pending.\"\n  #{:segment :site-pc :pc :frames :regs :live :continuation :dest :resume-mode\n    :format :hash :image :images :store-of :stack})\n\n\n(defn- canonical-env\n  [cx seg pc frames store-of]\n  (env-of seg pc (:free-env cx) (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(canonical-value cx %) f)) frames) store-of))\n\n\n(defn- register-window\n  \"§4.2 step 4: `{virt(site, s) V}` over the entry's `[s V]` pairs.\"\n  [cx seg site regs]\n  (into {} (map (fn [[s x]] [(virt seg site s) (canonical-value cx x)])) regs))\n\n\n(defn- register-kframe\n  \"§4.2 step 6, one frame independently: its own image row and A, `rd`\n   from A, never the physical `:dest`.\"\n  [cx f]\n  (let [[seg pc] (image-pc :register (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:return-pc f))]\n    (safepoint! seg pc false)\n    {:type :return :segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n     :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames f) (:store-of f))\n     :window (register-window cx seg (dec pc) (:regs f))\n     :rd (code/rd (inst seg (dec pc)))}))\n\n\n(defn- lift-register\n  [cx entry]\n  (let [[seg pc] (image-pc :register (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:pc entry))\n        tail? (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\n        _ (safepoint! seg pc tail?)\n        k (mapv #(register-kframe cx %) (:continuation entry))]\n    (if tail?\n      {:segment (:address seg) :site (dec pc) :k k :deliver {:deliver :return}}\n      {:segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n       :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames entry) (:store-of entry))\n       :window (register-window cx seg (dec pc) (:regs entry))\n       :k k\n       :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd (code/rd (inst seg (dec pc)))}})))\n\n\n(defn slices\n  \"§4.3's K slices of operand stack `st` under return frames whose bases\n   are `bases`, outermost first: `St[b(i-1), b(i))` per frame with\n   `b(-1) = 0`, then the current activation's `St[b(m-1), n)`.\"\n  [st bases]\n  (let [bounds (into [0] bases)]\n    (conj (mapv (fn [lo hi] (subvec st lo hi)) bounds (rest bounds))\n          (subvec st (peek bounds) (count st)))))\n\n\n(defn- slice-window\n  \"`(zipmap (stack-layout (dec pc)) slice)`; the two have equal length.\"\n  [cx seg pc slice]\n  (let [layout (stack-layout seg (dec pc))]\n    (when-not (= (count layout) (count slice))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :stack-layout {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/layout layout :yin.k/slice (count slice)}))\n    (zipmap layout (map #(canonical-value cx %) slice))))\n\n\n(defn- stack-site\n  \"`[segment site]`: the A pc of the parking instruction before absolute\n   stack resume pc `abs`.\"\n  [cx abs]\n  (let [[seg rel] (image-pc :stack (:kernel cx) (:space cx) abs)]\n    [seg (h->a seg (dec rel))]))\n\n\n(defn- lift-stack\n  [cx entry]\n  (let [st (vec (:stack entry))\n        frames (vec (:continuation entry))\n        bases (mapv :stack-base frames)\n        _ (when-not (and (every? integer? bases) (apply <= 0 (conj bases (count st))))\n            (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :stack-base {:yin.k/bases bases}))\n        parts (slices st bases)\n        [seg site] (stack-site cx (:pc entry))\n        tail? (code/tail-call? (inst seg site))\n        _ (safepoint! seg (inc site) tail?)\n        k (mapv (fn [f slice]\n                  (let [[fseg fsite] (stack-site cx (:return-pc f))\n                        pc (inc fsite)]\n                    (safepoint! fseg pc false)\n                    {:type :return :segment (:address fseg) :pc pc\n                     :env (canonical-env cx fseg pc (:frames f) (:store-of f))\n                     :window (slice-window cx fseg pc slice)\n                     :rd (code/rd (inst fseg fsite))}))\n                frames parts)]\n    (if tail?\n      ;; frozen §2.4: the current frames, store-of and slice are dead\n      {:segment (:address seg) :site site :k k :deliver {:deliver :return}}\n      (let [pc (inc site)]\n        {:segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n         :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames entry) (:store-of entry))\n         :window (slice-window cx seg pc (peek parts))\n         :k k\n         :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd (code/rd (inst seg site))}}))))\n\n\n(defn lift-state\n  \"A kernel's wait entry, parked record or reified payload as the\n   canonical act or tail payload (§4.2, §4.3), engine fields carried.\"\n  [cx entry]\n  (let [fields (apply dissoc entry kernel-keys)]\n    (merge (cond-> fields (contains? fields :datom) (update :datom #(canonical-value cx %)))\n           (if (= :stack (:kind cx)) (lift-stack cx entry) (lift-register cx entry)))))\n\n\n(defn lift-context\n  \"The lift context of kernel `k` over `space`; positional closures and\n   kernel continuations are reminted under `owner`.\"\n  [k space owner]\n  (assoc {} :kind (kernel-kind k) :kernel k :space space :free-env (or (:free-env k) {}) :owner owner))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Lower: a canonical act or tail into a kernel\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- lower-frames\n  [lx seg pc env]\n  (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(positional-value lx %) f)) (frames-of seg pc env)))\n\n\n(defn- payload-segment\n  [lx p]\n  (segment-of (:space lx) (address-of lx (:segment p))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-regs\n  \"`(sort-by first [[phys(v) V] …])` over window `w`.\"\n  [lx seg site w]\n  (vec (sort-by first (map (fn [[x v]] [(phys seg site x) (positional-value lx v)]) w))))\n\n\n(defn- register-k\n  [lx k]\n  (mapv (fn [f]\n          (let [seg (payload-segment lx f)\n                off (offset :register (:kernel lx) seg)\n                pc (:pc f)\n                regs (lower-regs lx seg (dec pc) (:window f))\n                store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env f))]\n            (cond-> {:site-pc (+ off pc -1) :return-pc (+ off pc)\n                     :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env f))\n                     :regs regs :live (mapv first regs)\n                     :dest (phys seg (dec pc) (:rd f))}\n              (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))\n        k))\n\n\n(defn- lower-register\n  [lx p fill]\n  (let [k (:kernel lx)\n        seg (payload-segment lx p)\n        off (offset :register k seg)\n        common (cond-> {:segment (:segment k) :format register/format-tag :hash (:hash k)\n                        :image (:register-id seg) :continuation (register-k lx (:k p))}\n                 (< 1 (count (:images k))) (assoc :images (:images k)))]\n    (if (contains? p :site)\n      (cond-> (merge common {:site-pc (+ off (:site p)) :pc (+ off (:site p) 1)\n                             :frames (get fill :frames []) :regs [] :live [] :dest nil\n                             :resume-mode :return-result})\n        (some? (:store-of fill)) (assoc :store-of (:store-of fill)))\n      (let [pc (:pc p)\n            regs (lower-regs lx seg (dec pc) (:window p))\n            store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env p))]\n        (cond-> (merge common {:site-pc (+ off pc -1) :pc (+ off pc)\n                               :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env p))\n                               :regs regs :live (mapv first regs)\n                               :dest (phys seg (dec pc) (get-in p [:deliver :rd]))\n                               :resume-mode :write-result})\n          (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n\n\n(defn- layout-slice\n  \"`(mapv W (stack-layout (dec pc)))`, every member present in W.\"\n  [lx seg pc w]\n  (mapv (fn [x]\n          (when-not (contains? w x)\n            (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable :window-missing {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/register x}))\n          (positional-value lx (get w x)))\n        (stack-layout seg (dec pc))))\n\n\n(defn- stack-k\n  \"`[frames stack]`: each return frame's slice appended in order, its base\n   the cumulative length through its own slice (§4.3), `b(i) = b(i-1) +\n   |slice(i)|`.\"\n  [lx k]\n  (reduce (fn [[frames st] f]\n            (let [seg (payload-segment lx f)\n                  pc (:pc f)\n                  st (into st (layout-slice lx seg pc (:window f)))\n                  store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env f))]\n              [(conj frames (cond-> {:return-pc (+ (offset :stack (:kernel lx) seg) (a->h seg (dec pc)) 1)\n                                     :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env f))\n                                     :stack-base (count st)}\n                              (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of)))\n               st]))\n          [[] []]\n          k))\n\n\n(defn- lower-stack\n  [lx p fill]\n  (let [k (:kernel lx)\n        seg (payload-segment lx p)\n        off (offset :stack k seg)\n        [frames st] (stack-k lx (:k p))\n        common {:segment (:segment k) :format stack/format-tag :hash (:hash k) :image (:stack-id seg)\n                :continuation frames}]\n    (if (contains? p :site)\n      (cond-> (merge common {:pc (+ off (a->h seg (:site p)) 1) :resume-mode :return-result\n                             :stack st :frames (get fill :frames [])})\n        (some? (:store-of fill)) (assoc :store-of (:store-of fill)))\n      (let [pc (:pc p)\n            store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env p))]\n        (cond-> (merge common {:pc (+ off (a->h seg (dec pc)) 1)\n                               :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env p))\n                               :stack (into st (layout-slice lx seg pc (:window p)))})\n          (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private canonical-keys\n  #{:segment :pc :site :env :window :k :deliver :type :id})\n\n\n(defn lower-state\n  \"Canonical act or tail payload `p` as the receiving kernel's entry\n   (§4.2, §4.3), engine fields carried. `fill` gives a lowered tail's\n   `:frames`/`:store-of` (default `[]`/nil), which the return transition\n   replaces unread (§5.6 item 8).\"\n  ([lx p] (lower-state lx p {}))\n  ([lx p fill]\n   (let [fields (apply dissoc p canonical-keys)]\n     (merge (cond-> fields (contains? fields :datom) (update :datom #(positional-value lx %)))\n            (if (= :stack (:kind lx)) (lower-stack lx p fill) (lower-register lx p fill))))))\n\n\n(defn lower-context\n  \"The lower context into kernel `k` over `space`; `address` maps a\n   payload's or closure's `:segment` to A (default: it is A).\"\n  ([k space] (lower-context k space identity))\n  ([k space address]\n   (assoc {} :kind (kernel-kind k) :kernel k :space space :free-env (or (:free-env k) {})\n          :owner (:owner k) :address address)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Tasks\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn canonical-task\n  \"Quiescent kernel `k` presented as semantic-register machine `template`\n   (a fresh machine of the same composition) for `rows/lift-task`: code\n   by A from `space`, every wait, parked record and value reconstructed\n   through the layout; resources, stores and counters carried. A running\n   kernel is `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; install children are not carried\n   by this phase's layouts.\"\n  [k space template]\n  (when (engine/active-continuation? k)\n    (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc (:pc k)}))\n  (when (seq (:installs k))\n    (refuse! :yin.k/unsupported :installs {:yin.k/names (vec (keys (:installs k)))}))\n  (let [cx (lift-context k space (:owner template))\n        conv #(canonical-value cx %)\n        parked (into {} (map (fn [[id rec]] [id (assoc (lift-state cx rec) :type :parked-continuation :id id)]))\n                     (:parked k))\n        value (:value k)\n        parked-value? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? parked (:id value)))\n        code (into {} (map (fn [[a s]] [a (assoc {} :vector (:vector s) :address a :analysis (:analysis s))]))\n                   (:segments space))]\n    (assoc template\n           :code code\n           :code-aliases (into {} (map (fn [a] [a a])) (keys code))\n           :program nil :control nil :window {} :k nil\n           :resources (:resources k)\n           :capability-secret (:capability-secret k)\n           :free-env (:free-env k)\n           :env (or (:free-env k) {})\n           :store (conv (:store k))\n           :module-stores (conv (or (:module-stores k) {}))\n           :parked parked\n           :wait-set (mapv #(lift-state cx %) (:wait-set k))\n           :ready-queue (:ready-queue k)\n           :value (if parked-value? (get parked (:id value)) (conv value))\n           :id-counter (:id-counter k)\n           :installs {}\n           :halted? (:halted? k)\n           :blocked? (:blocked? k))))\n\n\n(defn lift-task\n  \"§7.1 for a de Bruijn kernel: `rows/lift-task` over its canonical\n   presentation. `template` is a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n   kernel's composition; opts as rows/lift-task's.\"\n  [k space template serve! opts]\n  (rows/lift-task (canonical-task k space template) serve! opts))\n\n\n(defn attach-space\n  \"Kernel `k` holding the derived image of every segment of `space`, in\n   A order (§7.2: derive and attach the image for each A).\"\n  [k space]\n  (let [kind (kernel-kind k)]\n    (reduce (fn [k a]\n              (let [seg (segment-of space a)]\n                (if (= :stack kind)\n                  (stack/attach-image k (:stack seg) vm/stack-contract)\n                  (register/attach-image k (:register seg) vm/register-contract))))\n            k\n            (sort-by str (keys (:segments space))))))\n\n\n(defn machine-space\n  \"The space of the A vectors semantic-register machine `m` holds, and\n   the map from its segment ids to A.\"\n  [m]\n  [(space (map :vector (vals (:code m))))\n   (fn [seg] (or (get-in m [:code seg :address]) (when (contains? (:code-aliases m) seg) seg)))])\n\n\n(defn kernel-task\n  \"Step 12 for a de Bruijn receiver: semantic-register machine `m` (what\n   `rows/lower-task` restored) as fresh kernel `k` of the same\n   composition: every image derived and attached, the free environment\n   set, every wait, parked record and value lowered through the layout.\n   Delivers nothing, runs nothing.\"\n  [m k]\n  (let [[sp address] (machine-space m)\n        k (attach-space k sp)\n        lx (lower-context k sp address)\n        conv #(positional-value lx %)\n        parked (into {} (map (fn [[id rec]] [id (assoc (lower-state lx rec) :type :parked-continuation :id id)]))\n                     (:parked m))\n        value (:value m)\n        parked-value? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? parked (:id value)))]\n    (assoc k\n           :resources (:resources m)\n           :free-env (:free-env m)\n           :store (conv (:store m))\n           :module-stores (conv (or (:module-stores m) {}))\n           :parked parked\n           :wait-set (mapv #(lower-state lx %) (:wait-set m))\n           :ready-queue []\n           :value (if parked-value? (get parked (:id value)) (conv value))\n           :id-counter (:id-counter m)\n           :halted? (:halted? m)\n           :blocked? (:blocked? m))))\n\n\n(defn- lexical-names\n  \"The names the chain binds at `pc` of `v`.\"\n  [v pc]\n  (let [bodies (code/body-ranges v)]\n    (loop [b (code/body-index bodies pc) out #{}]\n      (if-let [owner (:owner (nth bodies b))]\n        (recur (code/body-index bodies owner) (into out (nth (nth v owner) 2)))\n        out))))\n\n\n(declare state-prim)\n\n\n(defn- value-prim\n  \"The path to the first `:prim` row carrier value `x` reaches as kernel\n   payload data: through guest collections, a closure's lexical bindings\n   (its positional frames) and a capture's state; or nil.\"\n  [code x path]\n  (when (and (vector? x) (= :row (first x)))\n    (let [n (second x) ss (:slots n)]\n      (case (:kind n)\n        :prim path\n        (:vec :list :set :map) (some (fn [[i y]] (value-prim code y (conj path i))) (map-indexed vector ss))\n        :closure (let [[a entry _ bindings] ss\n                       v (get code a)\n                       owner (when v (some (fn [pc]\n                                             (let [t (nth v pc)]\n                                               (when (and (= :closure (nth t 0)) (= entry (nth t 3))) pc)))\n                                           (range (count v))))\n                       names (if owner (lexical-names v owner) #{})]\n                   (some (fn [[s y]] (when (contains? names s) (value-prim code y (conj path s))))\n                         (partition 2 (:slots bindings))))\n        :reified (state-prim code (first ss) (conj path 0))\n        nil))))\n\n\n(defn- frame-prim\n  \"A frame's window and lexical bindings (§4.4: the free part is the\n   kernel's :free-env, never payload data).\"\n  [code a pc e w path]\n  (let [names (lexical-names (get code a) pc)]\n    (or (some (fn [[r y]] (value-prim code y (conj path :window r))) (partition 2 (:slots w)))\n        (some (fn [[sym y]] (when (contains? names sym) (value-prim code y (conj path :env sym))))\n              (partition 2 (:slots (first (:slots e))))))))\n\n\n(defn- state-prim\n  [code n path]\n  (let [kframes (fn [k]\n                  (some (fn [[i f]]\n                          (let [[a pc e w] (:slots f)]\n                            (frame-prim code a pc e w (conj path :k i))))\n                        (map-indexed vector (:slots k))))\n        [a pc e w k] (:slots n)]\n    (case (:kind n)\n      :act (or (frame-prim code a pc e w path) (kframes k))\n      :tail (kframes e)\n      nil)))\n\n\n(defn lower-defect\n  \"What a kernel of `kind` cannot hold, judged on decoded task `task`\n   before anything is attached: install children (not carried by this\n   phase's layouts), and for the register kernel a primitive function in\n   the payload data of a wait or parked state (a window, a lexical\n   binding, or reached through them), which its restore refuses as\n   `:continuation-registers` (`vm/machine-data?`). nil when it can.\"\n  [task kind]\n  (let [slots (:slots task)\n        code (nth slots 11)]\n    (cond\n      (seq (nth slots 12))\n      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :installs)\n\n      (= :register kind)\n      (when-let [path (or (some (fn [[i w]] (state-prim code (first (:slots w)) [:frames i]))\n                                (map-indexed vector (nth slots 13)))\n                          (some (fn [[p st]] (state-prim code st [:parked p]))\n                                (partition 2 (:slots (nth slots 8)))))]\n        (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :continuation-registers :yin.k/path path))\n\n      :else nil)))\n\n\n(defn lower-task\n  \"§7.2 into a de Bruijn kernel: decode `wire`, refuse what kernel `k`\n   cannot hold (`lower-defect`) before any attach, then `rows/lower-task`\n   into `scratch` (a fresh semantic-register machine of the same\n   composition: the carrier's steps 1-11 and restore) and `kernel-task`\n   into `k`. Throws the first refusal as ex-data.\"\n  ([scratch k wire attach!] (lower-task scratch k wire attach! {}))\n  ([scratch k wire attach! opts]\n   (let [task (rows/decode wire (merge rows/default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n     (when (= :task (:kind task))\n       (when-let [d (lower-defect task (kernel-kind k))]\n         (throw (ex-info \"Layout refused\" d))))\n     (kernel-task (rows/lower-task scratch wire attach! opts) k))))\n","numLines":899,"startLine":1,"totalLines":899}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P3PSZmz2zmnjNUjXnzsT6j","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
