{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019XqxHmcXr3LsYhKAbvceFp","type":"tool_result","content":"1727\t## 11. Owner questions\n1728\t\n1729\t**None.** The reviewer accepted the engine-less profile and rejected the\n1730\tmerged-`E` free environment; both are now settled in the text. Nothing\n1731\tremaining is owner-level.\n1732\t\n1733\t---\n1734\t\n1735\t## 12. Portability notes for the implementer\n1736\t\n1737\t1. **Nil-valued window keys (Dart, Node).** The window is built with\n1738\t   `select-keys` and encoded as `[r [:lit nil]]`; never filter `some?`\n1739\t   values; `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member` over row 22\n1740\t   (`(pair nil (next-of c))`, the nil operand evaluated before the read)\n1741\t   is the canary. Membership is always by `contains?`/key sets, never\n1742\t   `(get W r)`.\n1743\t2. **`for` over large seqs (Dart).** Row sets of the C4 modules run to\n1744\t   thousands of rows; build with `mapv`/`into`/`reduce`.\n1745\t3. **Reader whitespace before closers (Dart).** Pinned row sets are\n1746\t   Clojure data in `.cljc`, never EDN strings.\n1747\t4. **Duplicate protocol params (Dart).** `gc-children [_ _x]`\n1748\t   (`srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:386`); any new protocol method\n1749\t   in `layout` likewise.\n1750\t5. **Multi-key `assoc` on nil (Dart).** Frames and windows start from\n1751\t   `{}` (`handoff.cljc:1455-1457` records the trap).\n1752\t6. **Reader conditionals.** `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`\n1753\t   with `:cljd` first; `:clj`-only source-reading tests as `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`.\n1754\t7. **Private var access (Dart).** Every function named in §8 is public;\n1755\t   no `#'`.\n1756\t8. **Sorted keys.** Window and bindings rows are sorted by Jing\n1757\t   canonical bytes of the key, never by host `sort` on mixed types.\n1758\t9. **Numeric classes (Node).** `pc`, `rd`, `r`, `site` are exact\n1759\t   integers; compare with `cbor/numeric-kind` before `=` on wire values\n1760\t   (`ucf/profile-engine`, `ucf.cljc:77-91`, is the template).\n1761\t10. **Fresh worktree.** `mise trust` and `npm ci` before the Node lane."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da6a8ed-da80-4f95-b938-953b362e5554","uuid":"f032f869-a499-49ac-b929-880f3260bd5f","timestamp":"2026-10-12T18:26:25.994Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"## 11. Owner questions\n\n**None.** The reviewer accepted the engine-less profile and rejected the\nmerged-`E` free environment; both are now settled in the text. Nothing\nremaining is owner-level.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Portability notes for the implementer\n\n1. **Nil-valued window keys (Dart, Node).** The window is built with\n   `select-keys` and encoded as `[r [:lit nil]]`; never filter `some?`\n   values; `frame-test/nil-valued-register-is-a-member` over row 22\n   (`(pair nil (next-of c))`, the nil operand evaluated before the read)\n   is the canary. Membership is always by `contains?`/key sets, never\n   `(get W r)`.\n2. **`for` over large seqs (Dart).** Row sets of the C4 modules run to\n   thousands of rows; build with `mapv`/`into`/`reduce`.\n3. **Reader whitespace before closers (Dart).** Pinned row sets are\n   Clojure data in `.cljc`, never EDN strings.\n4. **Duplicate protocol params (Dart).** `gc-children [_ _x]`\n   (`srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc:386`); any new protocol method\n   in `layout` likewise.\n5. **Multi-key `assoc` on nil (Dart).** Frames and windows start from\n   `{}` (`handoff.cljc:1455-1457` records the trap).\n6. **Reader conditionals.** `#?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default)`\n   with `:cljd` first; `:clj`-only source-reading tests as `#?(:cljd nil :clj …)`.\n7. **Private var access (Dart).** Every function named in §8 is public;\n   no `#'`.\n8. **Sorted keys.** Window and bindings rows are sorted by Jing\n   canonical bytes of the key, never by host `sort` on mixed types.\n9. **Numeric classes (Node).** `pc`, `rd`, `r`, `site` are exact\n   integers; compare with `cbor/numeric-kind` before `=` on wire values\n   (`ucf/profile-engine`, `ucf.cljc:77-91`, is the template).\n10. **Fresh worktree.** `mise trust` and `npm ci` before the Node lane.","numLines":35,"startLine":1727,"totalLines":1762}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019XqxHmcXr3LsYhKAbvceFp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
