{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RCDUEYCc9Ha6EnabvSEzRd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n2\t  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n3\t   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n4\t\n5\t   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n6\t   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n7\t   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n8\t   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n9\t   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n10\t   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n11\t   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n12\t   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n13\t   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n14\t\n15\t   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n16\t   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n17\t   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n18\t   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n19\t   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n20\t   layout refusals close the file.\"\n21\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n22\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n23\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n24\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n25\t            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n26\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n27\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n28\t            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n29\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n30\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n31\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n32\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n33\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n34\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n35\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n36\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n37\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n38\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n39\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n40\t            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n41\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n42\t            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n43\t\n44\t\n45\t;; =============================================================================\n46\t;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n47\t;; =============================================================================\n48\t\n49\t(def source-index\n50\t  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n51\t   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n52\t  (atom {}))\n53\t\n54\t\n55\t(def code-index\n56\t  \"{A v}: every vector this harness projects, for the layouts' spaces.\"\n57\t  (atom {}))\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(defn project\n61\t  [ast]\n62\t  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))\n63\t        a (jing/segment-key v)]\n64\t    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n65\t    (swap! code-index assoc a v)\n66\t    v))\n67\t\n68\t\n69\t(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n70\t\n71\t\n72\t(def ^:dynamic *lane*\n73\t  \"The kernel a world is built on: :semantic-register (the reference\n74\t   lane), or :stack or :register, which run A's derived image and lift\n75\t   and lower through the layouts (§5.3).\"\n76\t  :semantic-register)\n77\t\n78\t\n79\t(def lanes [:semantic-register :stack :register])\n80\t\n81\t\n82\t(defn- composition\n83\t  [opts]\n84\t  (merge {:make-stream tu/make-stream :capability-secret tu/secret\n85\t          :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))\n86\t          :modules stream-modules}\n87\t         opts))\n88\t\n89\t\n90\t(defn- kernel-opts\n91\t  \"A de Bruijn kernel's options for the same composition: the full\n92\t   primitive table, and the initial environment as :free-env.\"\n93\t  [opts]\n94\t  (cond-> (assoc (dissoc (composition opts) :env) :primitives vm/primitives)\n95\t    (contains? opts :env) (assoc :free-env (:env opts))))\n96\t\n97\t\n98\t(defn machine\n99\t  ([] (machine {}))\n100\t  ([opts]\n101\t   (case *lane*\n102\t     :semantic-register (sr/create-vm (composition opts))\n103\t     :stack (dvm/create-vm [] (kernel-opts opts))\n104\t     :register (rvm/create-vm (assoc {} :bodies [] :instructions []) (kernel-opts opts)))))\n105\t\n106\t\n107\t(defn lane-of\n108\t  [m]\n109\t  (let [f (:format (module/link-format m))]\n110\t    (cond (= dvm/format-tag f) :stack\n111\t          (= rvm/format-tag f) :register\n112\t          :else :semantic-register)))\n113\t\n114\t\n115\t(def segment-of\n116\t  \"layout/segment, once per A.\"\n117\t  (memoize layout/segment))\n118\t\n119\t\n120\t(defn kernel-space\n121\t  \"The layout space of the A vectors whose images de Bruijn kernel k holds.\"\n122\t  [k]\n123\t  (let [id (if (= :stack (lane-of k)) :stack-id :register-id)\n124\t        held (into #{} (map first) (:images k))]\n125\t    (layout/space (filter #(contains? held (id %)) (map segment-of (vals @code-index))))))\n126\t\n127\t\n128\t(defn- kernel-load\n129\t  \"Attach v's derived image and start it at its row, beside whatever the\n130\t   kernel already holds: parked records keep naming their own rows.\"\n131\t  [k v]\n132\t  (let [kind (lane-of k)\n133\t        sg (segment-of v)\n134\t        k (if (= :stack kind)\n135\t            (dvm/attach-image k (:stack sg) vm/stack-contract)\n136\t            (rvm/attach-image k (:register sg) vm/register-contract))\n137\t        k (assoc k :pc (layout/offset kind k sg) :frames [] :continuation [] :store-of nil\n138\t                 :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)]\n139\t    (if (= :stack kind)\n140\t      (assoc k :stack [])\n141\t      (assoc k :registers (vec (repeat (:registers (first (:bodies (:register sg)))) nil))))))\n142\t\n143\t\n144\t(defn load-program\n145\t  [m ast]\n146\t  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n147\t    (sr/load-vector m (project ast) code/contract)\n148\t    (kernel-load m (project ast))))\n149\t\n150\t\n151\t(defn lane-closure\n152\t  \"Canonical closure payload c, its :segment an A, as machine m's value.\"\n153\t  [m c]\n154\t  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n155\t    (values/closure (:owner m) (update c :segment #(get (:code-aliases m) %)))\n156\t    (layout/positional-value (layout/lower-context m (kernel-space m)) (values/closure (:owner m) c))))\n157\t\n158\t\n159\t(defn lift-opts\n160\t  []\n161\t  {:source-index @source-index})\n162\t\n163\t\n164\t(defn error\n165\t  [f]\n166\t  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n167\t\n168\t\n169\t;; =============================================================================\n170\t;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n171\t;; =============================================================================\n172\t\n173\t(defn cat-of\n174\t  [p q]\n175\t  (s/app (s/v 'cat) p q))\n176\t\n177\t\n178\t(defn with-cat\n179\t  [ast]\n180\t  (s/let1 'cat (s/lam ['p 'q] (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/v 'p) (s/v 'q))) ast))\n181\t\n182\t\n183\t(defn nest\n184\t  [d op]\n185\t  (if (zero? d) op (cat-of (s/lit [d]) (s/app (s/lam ['x] (nest (dec d) op)) (s/lit d)))))\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t(def segments\n189\t  \"[label wrap expected-of-bare-result] (§5.2).\"\n190\t  [[:bare identity identity]\n191\t   [:operand #(cat-of (s/lit [:operand]) %) (fn [r] [:operand r])]\n192\t   [:depth-3 #(nest 3 %) (fn [r] [3 [2 [1 r]]])]\n193\t   [:captured #(s/let1 'k (s/lit :captured)\n194\t                       (s/let1 'f (s/lam ['y] (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k)) (s/v 'y)) %))\n195\t                               (s/app (s/v 'f) (s/lit :arg))))\n196\t    (fn [r] [:captured :arg r])]])\n197\t\n198\t\n199\t(defn with-stream\n200\t  [body]\n201\t  (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4} (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's)) body)))\n202\t\n203\t\n204\t(defn tail\n205\t  [ast]\n206\t  (assoc ast :tail? true))\n207\t\n208\t\n209\t(defn normalize\n210\t  [x]\n211\t  (cond\n212\t    (values/continuation? x) :continuation\n213\t    (values/closure? x) :closure\n214\t    (vector? x) (mapv normalize x)\n215\t    (seq? x) (apply list (map normalize x))\n216\t    (set? x) (into #{} (map normalize) x)\n217\t    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(normalize k) (normalize v)])) x)\n218\t    :else x))\n219\t\n220\t\n221\t;; =============================================================================\n222\t;; The rows of §5.2: one builder each, answering the parked machine\n223\t;; =============================================================================\n224\t;;\n225\t;; A world: :machine, :kind, :reason (blocked rows), :steps (each followed by\n226\t;; a drive) or :resume, :finish (records the effect trace), :trace, and\n227\t;; :receiver (fresh opts and a finish for the receiver's own composition).\n228\t\n229\t(defn reader\n230\t  \"A reader parked on (next-of c); :pre values are appended and the\n231\t   machine re-run first.\"\n232\t  ([wrap op] (reader wrap op [] \"B\" {}))\n233\t  ([wrap op pre value opts]\n234\t   (let [m0 (vm/run (load-program (machine opts) (with-stream (with-cat (wrap op)))))\n235\t         src (s/stream-of m0)\n236\t         m (reduce (fn [m x] (stream/append! src x) (vm/run m)) m0 pre)]\n237\t     {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :next :steps [#(stream/append! src value)] :trace (atom [])})))\n238\t\n239\t\n240\t(defn writer\n241\t  [wrap]\n242\t  (let [trace (atom [])\n243\t        w (support/one-slot-stream \"w\")\n244\t        _ (stream/append! w :warmed)\n245\t        m0 (load-program (machine) (with-cat (wrap {:type :stream/put :target (s/v 'w) :val (s/lit \"v\")})))\n246\t        [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n247\t        take! #(swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next w 0)))]\n248\t    {:machine (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref})) :kind :blocked :reason :put :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n249\t     :steps [take!] :finish take! :trace trace}))\n250\t\n251\t\n252\t(defn own-call-pair\n253\t  [trace]\n254\t  (let [own-in (s/ring 8) own-out (s/ring 8)]\n255\t    {:opts {:call-in own-in :call-out own-out :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest own-out :test)}\n256\t     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain own-in))}))\n257\t\n258\t\n259\t(defn caller\n260\t  [wrap call-in call-out]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da6a8ed-da80-4f95-b938-953b362e5554","uuid":"370ae03f-4522-451a-b69e-5378bb00999a","timestamp":"2026-10-12T18:26:28.743Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c/test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n\n   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n\n   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n   layout refusals close the file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def source-index\n  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(def code-index\n  \"{A v}: every vector this harness projects, for the layouts' spaces.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(defn project\n  [ast]\n  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))\n        a (jing/segment-key v)]\n    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n    (swap! code-index assoc a v)\n    v))\n\n\n(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n\n\n(def ^:dynamic *lane*\n  \"The kernel a world is built on: :semantic-register (the reference\n   lane), or :stack or :register, which run A's derived image and lift\n   and lower through the layouts (§5.3).\"\n  :semantic-register)\n\n\n(def lanes [:semantic-register :stack :register])\n\n\n(defn- composition\n  [opts]\n  (merge {:make-stream tu/make-stream :capability-secret tu/secret\n          :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))\n          :modules stream-modules}\n         opts))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-opts\n  \"A de Bruijn kernel's options for the same composition: the full\n   primitive table, and the initial environment as :free-env.\"\n  [opts]\n  (cond-> (assoc (dissoc (composition opts) :env) :primitives vm/primitives)\n    (contains? opts :env) (assoc :free-env (:env opts))))\n\n\n(defn machine\n  ([] (machine {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (case *lane*\n     :semantic-register (sr/create-vm (composition opts))\n     :stack (dvm/create-vm [] (kernel-opts opts))\n     :register (rvm/create-vm (assoc {} :bodies [] :instructions []) (kernel-opts opts)))))\n\n\n(defn lane-of\n  [m]\n  (let [f (:format (module/link-format m))]\n    (cond (= dvm/format-tag f) :stack\n          (= rvm/format-tag f) :register\n          :else :semantic-register)))\n\n\n(def segment-of\n  \"layout/segment, once per A.\"\n  (memoize layout/segment))\n\n\n(defn kernel-space\n  \"The layout space of the A vectors whose images de Bruijn kernel k holds.\"\n  [k]\n  (let [id (if (= :stack (lane-of k)) :stack-id :register-id)\n        held (into #{} (map first) (:images k))]\n    (layout/space (filter #(contains? held (id %)) (map segment-of (vals @code-index))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-load\n  \"Attach v's derived image and start it at its row, beside whatever the\n   kernel already holds: parked records keep naming their own rows.\"\n  [k v]\n  (let [kind (lane-of k)\n        sg (segment-of v)\n        k (if (= :stack kind)\n            (dvm/attach-image k (:stack sg) vm/stack-contract)\n            (rvm/attach-image k (:register sg) vm/register-contract))\n        k (assoc k :pc (layout/offset kind k sg) :frames [] :continuation [] :store-of nil\n                 :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)]\n    (if (= :stack kind)\n      (assoc k :stack [])\n      (assoc k :registers (vec (repeat (:registers (first (:bodies (:register sg)))) nil))))))\n\n\n(defn load-program\n  [m ast]\n  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n    (sr/load-vector m (project ast) code/contract)\n    (kernel-load m (project ast))))\n\n\n(defn lane-closure\n  \"Canonical closure payload c, its :segment an A, as machine m's value.\"\n  [m c]\n  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n    (values/closure (:owner m) (update c :segment #(get (:code-aliases m) %)))\n    (layout/positional-value (layout/lower-context m (kernel-space m)) (values/closure (:owner m) c))))\n\n\n(defn lift-opts\n  []\n  {:source-index @source-index})\n\n\n(defn error\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn cat-of\n  [p q]\n  (s/app (s/v 'cat) p q))\n\n\n(defn with-cat\n  [ast]\n  (s/let1 'cat (s/lam ['p 'q] (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/v 'p) (s/v 'q))) ast))\n\n\n(defn nest\n  [d op]\n  (if (zero? d) op (cat-of (s/lit [d]) (s/app (s/lam ['x] (nest (dec d) op)) (s/lit d)))))\n\n\n(def segments\n  \"[label wrap expected-of-bare-result] (§5.2).\"\n  [[:bare identity identity]\n   [:operand #(cat-of (s/lit [:operand]) %) (fn [r] [:operand r])]\n   [:depth-3 #(nest 3 %) (fn [r] [3 [2 [1 r]]])]\n   [:captured #(s/let1 'k (s/lit :captured)\n                       (s/let1 'f (s/lam ['y] (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k)) (s/v 'y)) %))\n                               (s/app (s/v 'f) (s/lit :arg))))\n    (fn [r] [:captured :arg r])]])\n\n\n(defn with-stream\n  [body]\n  (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4} (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's)) body)))\n\n\n(defn tail\n  [ast]\n  (assoc ast :tail? true))\n\n\n(defn normalize\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (values/continuation? x) :continuation\n    (values/closure? x) :closure\n    (vector? x) (mapv normalize x)\n    (seq? x) (apply list (map normalize x))\n    (set? x) (into #{} (map normalize) x)\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(normalize k) (normalize v)])) x)\n    :else x))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The rows of §5.2: one builder each, answering the parked machine\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; A world: :machine, :kind, :reason (blocked rows), :steps (each followed by\n;; a drive) or :resume, :finish (records the effect trace), :trace, and\n;; :receiver (fresh opts and a finish for the receiver's own composition).\n\n(defn reader\n  \"A reader parked on (next-of c); :pre values are appended and the\n   machine re-run first.\"\n  ([wrap op] (reader wrap op [] \"B\" {}))\n  ([wrap op pre value opts]\n   (let [m0 (vm/run (load-program (machine opts) (with-stream (with-cat (wrap op)))))\n         src (s/stream-of m0)\n         m (reduce (fn [m x] (stream/append! src x) (vm/run m)) m0 pre)]\n     {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :next :steps [#(stream/append! src value)] :trace (atom [])})))\n\n\n(defn writer\n  [wrap]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n        w (support/one-slot-stream \"w\")\n        _ (stream/append! w :warmed)\n        m0 (load-program (machine) (with-cat (wrap {:type :stream/put :target (s/v 'w) :val (s/lit \"v\")})))\n        [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n        take! #(swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next w 0)))]\n    {:machine (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref})) :kind :blocked :reason :put :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n     :steps [take!] :finish take! :trace trace}))\n\n\n(defn own-call-pair\n  [trace]\n  (let [own-in (s/ring 8) own-out (s/ring 8)]\n    {:opts {:call-in own-in :call-out own-out :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest own-out :test)}\n     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain own-in))}))\n\n\n(defn caller\n  [wrap call-in call-out]","numLines":260,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1672}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RCDUEYCc9Ha6EnabvSEzRd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
