{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B7gAWkTNyvBWWtpFZPKCFY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.layout-test\n2\t  \"Phase 6c acceptance 1-9 (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md\n3\t   §8.3): the register pairing and live sets, the register destination from\n4\t   A, the stack correspondence, operand layout and K slices, E\n5\t   reconstruction, closures both ways, and the unobservable fill of a\n6\t   lowered tail. The static items run over C, the B0 corpus and the\n7\t   phase-3 corpus (derive-test's wider C requires the Python ANTLR lane);\n8\t   the dynamic items run the harness's worlds on the de Bruijn lanes.\"\n9\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n10\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n11\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n12\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n13\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n14\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n15\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n16\t            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n17\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n18\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n19\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n20\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n21\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n22\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n23\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test :as h]\n24\t            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n25\t\n26\t\n27\t(def C\n28\t  \"[label ast]: the B0 corpus, the phase-3 corpus, then a tail call in\n29\t   operand position, whose dead layout syntax reads registers other than\n30\t   the call's own (phase-5 §6.3's last golden).\"\n31\t  (conj (into (mapv (fn [[label ast _]] [label ast]) b0/corpus) corpus/programs)\n32\t        [:tail-operand (corpus/app (corpus/v 'f) (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/v 'g) (corpus/v 'x))) (corpus/v 'y))]))\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t(defn projected\n36\t  [ast]\n37\t  (:vector (linearize/project ast)))\n38\t\n39\t\n40\t(defn reachable-pcs\n41\t  \"Every pc reachable from its body's start.\"\n42\t  [v]\n43\t  (into #{} (mapcat #(analysis/reachable v (:start %))) (code/body-ranges v)))\n44\t\n45\t\n46\t(defn boundary?\n47\t  [t]\n48\t  (contains? rcode/boundary-opcodes (nth t 0)))\n49\t\n50\t\n51\t(defn parking?\n52\t  \"A non-tail parking instruction (rule A1).\"\n53\t  [t]\n54\t  (or (contains? #{:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :park :current-continuation} (nth t 0))\n55\t      (and (= :call (nth t 0)) (not (code/tail-call? t)))))\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t;; =============================================================================\n59\t;; 1-2: the register kernel's static layout\n60\t;; =============================================================================\n61\t\n62\t(deftest register-pairing\n63\t  (let [checked (atom [0 0])]\n64\t    (doseq [[label ast] C]\n65\t      (testing (str label)\n66\t        (let [v (projected ast)\n67\t              sg (layout/segment v)\n68\t              bodies (:bodies sg)]\n69\t          ;; phys is total on every body's named virtuals and single-valued\n70\t          (doseq [[pc x s] (:pairs sg)]\n71\t            (is (= s (layout/phys sg pc x)) (str \"pc \" pc \" virtual \" x)))\n72\t          (doseq [b (range (count bodies))]\n73\t            (let [named (into #{} (keep (fn [[pc x]] (when (= b (code/body-index bodies pc)) x))) (:pairs sg))]\n74\t              (is (= named (set (keys (nth (:phys sg) b)))))))\n75\t          ;; virt is single-valued on live-out's physical image\n76\t          (doseq [p (sort (reachable-pcs v))\n77\t                  :when (boundary? (nth v p))]\n78\t            (let [lo (layout/live-out sg p)]\n79\t              (is (= (count lo) (count (set (map #(layout/phys sg p %) lo))))\n80\t                  (str \"distinct live virtuals hold distinct slots at pc \" p))\n81\t              (doseq [x lo]\n82\t                (is (= x (layout/virt sg p (layout/phys sg p x))))))\n83\t            (swap! checked update 1 inc))\n84\t          (swap! checked update 0 inc))))\n85\t    (is (= (count C) (first @checked)))\n86\t    (is (< 50 (second @checked)) \"reachable boundaries checked\")))\n87\t\n88\t\n89\t(deftest register-live-is-live-out\n90\t  (let [tails (atom 0)]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da6a8ed-da80-4f95-b938-953b362e5554","uuid":"08dd11e5-d440-4a02-be47-0db2b6126d33","timestamp":"2026-10-12T18:27:08.374Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p6c/test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.layout-test\n  \"Phase 6c acceptance 1-9 (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md\n   §8.3): the register pairing and live sets, the register destination from\n   A, the stack correspondence, operand layout and K slices, E\n   reconstruction, closures both ways, and the unobservable fill of a\n   lowered tail. The static items run over C, the B0 corpus and the\n   phase-3 corpus (derive-test's wider C requires the Python ANTLR lane);\n   the dynamic items run the harness's worlds on the de Bruijn lanes.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test :as h]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n\n\n(def C\n  \"[label ast]: the B0 corpus, the phase-3 corpus, then a tail call in\n   operand position, whose dead layout syntax reads registers other than\n   the call's own (phase-5 §6.3's last golden).\"\n  (conj (into (mapv (fn [[label ast _]] [label ast]) b0/corpus) corpus/programs)\n        [:tail-operand (corpus/app (corpus/v 'f) (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/v 'g) (corpus/v 'x))) (corpus/v 'y))]))\n\n\n(defn projected\n  [ast]\n  (:vector (linearize/project ast)))\n\n\n(defn reachable-pcs\n  \"Every pc reachable from its body's start.\"\n  [v]\n  (into #{} (mapcat #(analysis/reachable v (:start %))) (code/body-ranges v)))\n\n\n(defn boundary?\n  [t]\n  (contains? rcode/boundary-opcodes (nth t 0)))\n\n\n(defn parking?\n  \"A non-tail parking instruction (rule A1).\"\n  [t]\n  (or (contains? #{:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :park :current-continuation} (nth t 0))\n      (and (= :call (nth t 0)) (not (code/tail-call? t)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; 1-2: the register kernel's static layout\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest register-pairing\n  (let [checked (atom [0 0])]\n    (doseq [[label ast] C]\n      (testing (str label)\n        (let [v (projected ast)\n              sg (layout/segment v)\n              bodies (:bodies sg)]\n          ;; phys is total on every body's named virtuals and single-valued\n          (doseq [[pc x s] (:pairs sg)]\n            (is (= s (layout/phys sg pc x)) (str \"pc \" pc \" virtual \" x)))\n          (doseq [b (range (count bodies))]\n            (let [named (into #{} (keep (fn [[pc x]] (when (= b (code/body-index bodies pc)) x))) (:pairs sg))]\n              (is (= named (set (keys (nth (:phys sg) b)))))))\n          ;; virt is single-valued on live-out's physical image\n          (doseq [p (sort (reachable-pcs v))\n                  :when (boundary? (nth v p))]\n            (let [lo (layout/live-out sg p)]\n              (is (= (count lo) (count (set (map #(layout/phys sg p %) lo))))\n                  (str \"distinct live virtuals hold distinct slots at pc \" p))\n              (doseq [x lo]\n                (is (= x (layout/virt sg p (layout/phys sg p x))))))\n            (swap! checked update 1 inc))\n          (swap! checked update 0 inc))))\n    (is (= (count C) (first @checked)))\n    (is (< 50 (second @checked)) \"reachable boundaries checked\")))\n\n\n(deftest register-live-is-live-out\n  (let [tails (atom 0)]","numLines":90,"startLine":1,"totalLines":426}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01B7gAWkTNyvBWWtpFZPKCFY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
